1
00:00:03,857 --> 00:00:06,254
The Lives Of The Prophets, Part 1

2
00:00:06,746 --> 00:00:10,416
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

3
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:17,218
Adam(آدم), when he was created, Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ stroke his back,

4
00:00:18,281 --> 00:00:22,749
so all of the descendants of Adam(آدم) came out from the back of Adam(آدم).

5
00:00:24,487 --> 00:00:29,768
We don’t know in which form they came out, but they all fell down from his back, all of them.

6
00:00:31,570 --> 00:00:35,196
And Allah سبحانه وتعالى put some light between their eyes.

7
00:00:37,998 --> 00:00:39,665
Adam(آدم) said: “Who are they?”

8
00:00:40,419 --> 00:00:43,124
Allah سبحانه وتعالى said: “These are your descendants.”

9
00:00:45,179 --> 00:00:53,318
So Adam(آدم) looked at one of them and he saw some bright shining light between his eyes, and he liked him.

10
00:00:54,453 --> 00:00:56,119
So Adam(آدم) said: “Who is this?”

11
00:00:57,563 --> 00:00:59,201
Allah سبحانه وتعالى told him;

12
00:00:59,318 --> 00:01:04,770
“This is one of your descendants who’s gonna come in the end of time, his name is Dawud(داؤد).”

13
00:01:06,458 --> 00:01:10,995
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) Allah’s telling Adam(آدم): “This is Dawud(داؤد),” it’s towards the end of time.

14
00:01:11,495 --> 00:01:12,773
Where are we living then?

15
00:01:13,442 --> 00:01:14,309
Adam(آدم) said;

16
00:01:14,625 --> 00:01:15,541
كم عمره؟

17
00:01:15,752 --> 00:01:16,776
“What’s his age?”

18
00:01:17,712 --> 00:01:19,506
Allah سبحانه وتعالى said: “60 years old.”

19
00:01:20,014 --> 00:01:20,847
Adam(آدم) loved him.

20
00:01:21,141 --> 00:01:22,792
This is one of his children, one of his descendants.

21
00:01:22,863 --> 00:01:25,316
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) all of us are the children of Adam(آدم).

22
00:01:26,149 --> 00:01:29,742
He views us all as his children, his descendants.

23
00:01:30,425 --> 00:01:34,512
Even though there’s thousands of years between Adam(آدم) and Dawud(داود), but he loved him.

24
00:01:35,790 --> 00:01:39,289
So he told Allah سبحانه وتعالى: “O Allah, give him 40 years from my life.”

25
00:01:40,614 --> 00:01:43,741
He said: “O Allah, give him 40 years from my life.”

26
00:01:45,328 --> 00:01:47,248
Allah سبحانه وتعالى told Adam(آدم);

27
00:01:47,796 --> 00:01:50,582
“Then it would be written down and sealed.”

28
00:01:50,764 --> 00:01:52,277
In other words: “Are you sure?”

29
00:01:53,793 --> 00:01:55,380
Adam(آدم) said: “Yes.”

30
00:01:55,816 --> 00:01:58,840
So it was prescribed and sealed, that’s it.

31
00:02:00,761 --> 00:02:04,830
This happened when Adam(آدم) was created, very early in time.

32
00:02:05,591 --> 00:02:07,290
Adam(آدم) was supposed to live 1000 years,

33
00:02:07,330 --> 00:02:09,695
that’s the time Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ told Adam(آدم): “you would live.”

34
00:02:11,657 --> 00:02:15,586
So now Adam(آدم) is living in Duniya(دنيا‎) and years and years are passing by.

35
00:02:16,181 --> 00:02:21,887
Then, when he was 960 years old, the Angel of Death came to Adam(آدم)

36
00:02:22,697 --> 00:02:26,403
and told him: “Are you ready to die?” because the Angel of Death takes permission from the Ambiya(أنبياء).

37
00:02:26,832 --> 00:02:27,890
Are you ready to die?

38
00:02:28,310 --> 00:02:31,866
Adam(آدم) said: “I still have 40 years to live.

39
00:02:33,136 --> 00:02:36,893
Allah told me that I’m gonna live 1000 years, I still have 40 years to live.”

40
00:02:37,972 --> 00:02:43,222
The Angel of Death said: “Didn’t you give 40 years of your life to your son, Dawud(داؤد)?”

41
00:02:45,198 --> 00:02:46,333
Adam(آدم) denied.

42
00:02:47,532 --> 00:02:48,595
Adam(آدم) denied.

43
00:02:49,270 --> 00:02:51,624
This Hadith(حديث) is Sahih(صحيح). Adam(آدم) denied.

44
00:02:53,623 --> 00:02:54,925
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

45
00:02:55,036 --> 00:02:57,592
فجحد آدم فجحدت ذرّيته

46
00:02:58,028 --> 00:03:01,285
 “Adam(آدَم) denied, so the children of Adam(آدَم), they deny.”

47
00:03:01,848 --> 00:03:03,983
ونسي آدم فنسيت ذرّيته

48
00:03:04,023 --> 00:03:06,920
 “And Adam(آدَم) forgot, and his children forget.”

49
00:03:07,777 --> 00:03:09,801
وخطئ آدم فخطئت ذريته

50
00:03:09,841 --> 00:03:12,828
“And Adam(آدَم) made mistakes, and his children make mistakes.”

51
00:03:13,630 --> 00:03:15,019
Adam(آدم) forgot.

52
00:03:15,701 --> 00:03:19,534
See, sometimes we forget and that is human nature.

53
00:03:20,788 --> 00:03:24,750
And it is said that the name Insan(إنسان) - Insan(إنسان) comes from Nisyan(نسيان);

54
00:03:25,184 --> 00:03:27,700
Insan(إنسان) in Arabic comes from Nisyan(نسيان) which is forgetting.

55
00:03:28,041 --> 00:03:29,898
It’s a human nature; we forget,

56
00:03:30,795 --> 00:03:32,730
 and when we forget, we reject.

57
00:03:33,032 --> 00:03:36,024
Adam(آدم) denied - denied that he gave 40 years because he forgot.

58
00:03:36,191 --> 00:03:38,937
He wasn’t lying, we need to understand that, Adam(آدم) forgot.

59
00:03:39,611 --> 00:03:42,389
Adam(آدم) is a Nabi(نبي‎) of Allah سبحانه وتعالى, and the Ambiya(أنبياء) of Allah,

60
00:03:42,429 --> 00:03:43,540
معصومون عن كذب

61
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:48,324
Allah سبحانه وتعالى made them infallible from falling in the sins,

62
00:03:48,785 --> 00:03:51,753
so Adam(آدم) - he forgot that he gave this promise.

63
00:03:52,737 --> 00:03:57,985
Adam(آدم) forgot, and Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ forgave him, this was a mistake from Adam(آدم).

64
00:03:58,779 --> 00:03:59,993
And this is a Nabi(نبي‎) of Allah.

65
00:04:00,588 --> 00:04:06,601
Always in agreements that we have with each other and things that we say in our daily conversations, this thing happens again and again.

66
00:04:07,688 --> 00:04:10,476
I would say something today, you would come to me after a month

67
00:04:10,516 --> 00:04:13,294
and you would say: “You promised me so and so.” I tell you: “No, I didn’t.”

68
00:04:13,794 --> 00:04:18,089
You accuse me of lying. I’m not lying, I forgot, I did not lie.

69
00:04:18,581 --> 00:04:21,242
 We forget and that happens, and give excuse for your brothers.

70
00:04:21,282 --> 00:04:24,430
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: “Find 70 excuses for your brother.”

71
00:04:24,647 --> 00:04:25,978
No, we don’t find any excuses.

72
00:04:26,018 --> 00:04:31,192
“You’re lying, I’m sure that I told you so. You are a liar!”

73
00:04:31,248 --> 00:04:33,994
And you brand him as a liar for the rest of his life.

74
00:04:34,986 --> 00:04:38,666
Adam(آدم), and this is something big, this is something really big;

75
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:43,150
I mean, you promised 40 years of your life, this is a big thing - Adam(آدم) forgot.

76
00:04:43,547 --> 00:04:46,898
It’s human nature, you could forget major things.

77
00:04:47,784 --> 00:04:52,801
And on small details, if somebody forgets, it’s a big problem and a big deal.

78
00:04:53,465 --> 00:04:58,409
You know, let’s use these stories to learn some Akhlaq(أخلاق‎) also because we are in great need of Akhlaq(أخلاق‎).

79
00:04:59,235 --> 00:05:05,311
You don’t know Al-Ghaib(الغيب), you don't know, maybe there was a miscommunication, maybe they didn’t understand you,

80
00:05:05,692 --> 00:05:08,626
they forgot, they made a mistake, they misinterpreted.

81
00:05:08,810 --> 00:05:15,445
You can find, easily if you want, 70 excuses or more, if you want to.

82
00:05:17,381 --> 00:05:25,851
Adam(آدم) then submitted to the Will of Allah سبحانه وتعالى and he gave away his soul.

83
00:05:26,629 --> 00:05:31,905
And humans did not learn, these things are new for them,

84
00:05:32,492 --> 00:05:43,093
so the angels descended and they washed Sayyidina Adam(سيدنا آدم) SAW - witran(وترًا) - an odd number of times

85
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:46,854
and they dug the grave for Adam(آدم) the Mala’ikah(ملائكة)

86
00:05:47,870 --> 00:05:52,957
and they made it in the form of a Lahat(لهت) and they buried Sayyidina Adam عليه السّلام.

87
00:05:53,647 --> 00:05:56,060
The angels washed him and the angels buried him.

88
00:05:56,710 --> 00:05:59,576
This is our father Adam عليه السّلام.

89
00:06:00,227 --> 00:06:02,417
This is the end of his story.

90
00:06:03,354 --> 00:06:08,051
We ask Allah سبحانه وتعالى to bring us together with our father,

91
00:06:08,328 --> 00:06:09,368
في مستقر رحمته

92
00:06:09,408 --> 00:06:09,932
 In Jannah(جنة‎).

93
00:06:11,408 --> 00:06:12,289
Sayyidina Sheeth(سيدنا شيث‎),

94
00:06:12,789 --> 00:06:15,521
Sheeth(شيث‎) is one of the Ambiya(أنبياء) that are not mentioned in Qur'an.

95
00:06:17,862 --> 00:06:20,688
He’s a Nabi(نبي‎) that we know of from Sunnah(سنة‎).

96
00:06:22,156 --> 00:06:23,971
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

97
00:06:25,011 --> 00:06:31,599
أنزلت مائة صحيفة وأربع صحف منها خمسين على شيث

98
00:06:33,077 --> 00:06:42,479
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: “Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ has revealed the 104 scrolls, 50 of them on Sheeth(شيث).”

99
00:06:43,026 --> 00:06:46,660
Sayyidina Sheeth(سيدنا شيث) received revelation from Allah,

100
00:06:48,501 --> 00:06:53,199
and it is mentioned by some of the scholars that he is the son of Adam(آدم)

101
00:06:53,549 --> 00:06:59,804
and that Adam(آدم) gave him the responsibility of leading when he was passing away.

102
00:07:00,145 --> 00:07:06,945
So Adam(آدم) gave Wasiyyah(وصية) to Sheeth(شيث‎) to take care of the affairs of mankind.

103
00:07:07,469 --> 00:07:12,300
Sheeth(شيث‎) assumed responsibility after his father Adam(آدم).

104
00:07:12,475 --> 00:07:15,157
That’s almost all what we know about Sheeth(شيث‎).

105
00:07:15,816 --> 00:07:18,530
Following Sheeth(شيث‎) is Sayyidina Idris(سيدنا إدريس).

106
00:07:19,646 --> 00:07:25,959
Idris(إدريس), most of the scholars say, is a Nabi(نبي‎) that came between Sheeth(شيث‎) and Nuh(نوح).

107
00:07:27,658 --> 00:07:33,629
But there’s an opinion of Sayyidina Ibn Masʿud رضي الله عنه that Idris(إدريس) is the same Nabi(نبي‎) as Ilyas(إلياس‎),

108
00:07:34,692 --> 00:07:37,597
but that’s a lonely opinion of Sayyidina Ibn Masʿud(سيدنا ٱبن مسعود).

109
00:07:37,756 --> 00:07:43,585
The rest say that Idris(إدريس) is between Sayyidina Sheeth(سيدنا شيث) and Nuh(نوح).

110
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:48,061
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ did mention about Idris(إدريس) in Qur'an.

111
00:07:48,410 --> 00:07:49,502
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

112
00:07:49,542 --> 00:07:52,809
وَٱذْكُرْ فِى ٱلْكِتَـٰبِ إِدْرِيسَ ۚ

113
00:07:52,888 --> 00:07:56,886
إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ صِدِّيقًا نَّبِيًّا ۝

114
00:07:56,966 --> 00:08:01,752
وَرَفَعْنَـٰهُ مَكَانًا عَلِيًّا۝

115
00:08:01,823 --> 00:08:07,619
And remember in the book Idris(إدريس). He was a Siddeeq(صديق), truthful, and he was a Nabi(نَبِي).

116
00:08:08,032 --> 00:08:11,079
And We elevated him to a high level.

117
00:08:11,929 --> 00:08:18,841
That’s the extent of the knowledge, the accurate and sure knowledge that we have about Idris(إدريس).

118
00:08:19,603 --> 00:08:23,491
But, we have some stories about him from Al-Israʼiliyyat(الاسرائیلیات).

119
00:08:23,650 --> 00:08:29,404
And let me tell you what an Israʼiliyyat(اسرائیلیات‎) is as a definition that you will remember throughout this series.

120
00:08:30,507 --> 00:08:33,933
Israʼiliyyat(اسرائیلیات‎) are the stories of the People of the Book.

121
00:08:35,933 --> 00:08:39,507
We learn them through some of the Christians and the Jews who became Muslim.

122
00:08:41,428 --> 00:08:45,218
Some of the Christians and the Jews who became Muslim and they were scholars before,

123
00:08:45,384 --> 00:08:51,154
when they became Muslim, they brought some of these stories with them in Islam.

124
00:08:51,916 --> 00:08:58,751
Rasool Allah ﷺ has said in the beginning: “Do not speak about the stories of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل),” Al-Israʼiliyyat(الاسرائیلیات)

125
00:08:58,822 --> 00:09:02,194
these stories that come from the old scripture.

126
00:09:02,234 --> 00:09:04,005
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: “Don’t speak about them.”

127
00:09:04,188 --> 00:09:08,934
But then after that, towards the end of the life of Rasool Allah ﷺ, he said;

128
00:09:09,014 --> 00:09:10,672
حدثوا عن بني إسرائيل ولا حرج

129
00:09:10,910 --> 00:09:13,056
“Speak about Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل),” but then he said;

130
00:09:13,096 --> 00:09:15,176
لا تصدقوهم ولا تكذبوهم

131
00:09:15,343 --> 00:09:17,787
 “Do not believe them and do not disapprove.”

132
00:09:18,573 --> 00:09:22,590
Do not approve those stories and do not disapprove them.

133
00:09:22,963 --> 00:09:23,892
What does this mean?

134
00:09:24,360 --> 00:09:30,986
It means we could use them sometimes, but we should not take it as certain knowledge.

135
00:09:32,033 --> 00:09:37,367
And in the same time, if it does not contradict anything in Islam, we shouldn’t completely reject it.

136
00:09:38,176 --> 00:09:42,384
That’s why many of the scholars say it is safe to stay away from many of these stories.

137
00:09:43,209 --> 00:09:47,226
And that is what I’m gonna try to do, and whenever I do mention one of these stories,

138
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:51,306
I’ll mention it and mention to you that this is from Al-Israʼiliyyat(الاسرائیلیات) so that you know.

139
00:09:52,108 --> 00:09:53,695
And Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) did mention that

140
00:09:53,925 --> 00:09:58,259
we could use Al-Israʼiliyyat(الاسرائیلیات) as supplementary evidence, but not as primary evidence.

141
00:09:58,370 --> 00:10:01,322
You cannot use it as a Daleel(دليل), as a primary evidence,

142
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:03,672
but we could use it as Isti’nas(استئناس),

143
00:10:03,902 --> 00:10:10,700
you bring it along under an established thing in Islam, an established evidence, you could then use some of these stories.

144
00:10:11,177 --> 00:10:14,898
There is a story about the death of Sayyidina Idris(سيدنا إدريس) from Al-Israʼiliyyat(الاسرائیلیات).

145
00:10:15,033 --> 00:10:18,868
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ revealed to Idris(إدريس) and told him that

146
00:10:19,003 --> 00:10:24,725
“everyday, your deeds are equivalent to the good deeds of everybody else on the face of the earth.”

147
00:10:25,170 --> 00:10:27,397
With simple calculation, Sayyidina Idris(سيدنا إدريس) said;

148
00:10:28,612 --> 00:10:35,500
“If that is the case, then if I ask Allah سبحانه وتعالى to give me a longer life, I would be able to accumulate more good deeds.”

149
00:10:37,474 --> 00:10:42,665
So he told one of his friends - an angel who was a friend of his, he told him;

150
00:10:44,014 --> 00:10:50,148
“Why don’t we go and speak to the Angel of Death and see if we can go to Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ and ask him to give me a longer life?”

151
00:10:50,473 --> 00:10:53,592
So the angel said: “Okay, ride on my wings.”

152
00:10:54,354 --> 00:10:59,940
So Sayyidina Idris(سيدنا إدريس) went on the wings of this angel, and the angel carried him up in the Samawat(سماوات).

153
00:11:00,647 --> 00:11:03,208
So they passed the first heaven, As-Sama’ Al-Ula(السماء الأولى);

154
00:11:03,407 --> 00:11:05,296
and then the second heaven, As-Sama’ Ath-Thaniyah(السماء الثانية);

155
00:11:05,462 --> 00:11:07,193
the third heaven, As-Sama’ Ath-Thalithah(السماء الثالثة);

156
00:11:07,296 --> 00:11:09,073
the fourth heaven, As-Sama’ Ar-Rabiʿah(السماء الرابعة),

157
00:11:09,208 --> 00:11:13,020
and when they were going up, the Angel of Death was coming down.

158
00:11:14,187 --> 00:11:15,765
The Angel of Death said: “Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله),

159
00:11:15,948 --> 00:11:21,973
I just received an order from Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ to take the soul of Idris(إدريس) in the fourth heaven

160
00:11:22,616 --> 00:11:25,735
and I had no idea how I was gonna do it when he’s on Earth.”

161
00:11:26,751 --> 00:11:32,088
This angel speaking, with the Angel of Death looked on his back and saw that Idris(إدريس) has already passed away.

162
00:11:32,380 --> 00:11:38,420
They use this as an explanation of the Ayah(آية) where Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

163
00:11:38,460 --> 00:11:40,044
وَرَفَعْنَـٰهُ مَكَانًا عَلِيًّا۝

164
00:11:40,084 --> 00:11:42,190
We elevated him to a very high level.

165
00:11:42,745 --> 00:11:46,212
So Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ took his soul in the As-Sama’ Ar-Rabiʿ(سماء الرابع), in the fourth heaven,

166
00:11:46,752 --> 00:11:48,736
and elevated him to a very high level.

167
00:11:48,776 --> 00:11:52,017
Nobody passed away in that level except Sayyidina Idris(سيدنا إدريس),

168
00:11:52,249 --> 00:11:54,899
and that’s why Allah سبحانه وتعالى specifically said in Qur'an;

169
00:11:54,971 --> 00:11:56,234
وَرَفَعْنَـٰهُ مَكَانًا عَلِيًّا۝

170
00:11:56,274 --> 00:11:58,417
We have elevated him to a very high level.

171
00:11:59,615 --> 00:12:07,660
 And Rasool Allah ﷺ, in the authentic Hadith(حديث), did meet with Sayyidina Idris(سيدنا إدريس) in the fourth Sama(سماء), in the fourth heaven, in the Isra’ Wal-Miʿraj(إسراء والمعراج‎‎).

172
00:12:07,816 --> 00:12:11,885
In the Miʿraj(معراج‎‎), Rasool Allah ﷺ met with Idris(إدريس) in As-Sama’ Ar-Rabiʿah(السماء الرابعة).

173
00:12:12,435 --> 00:12:14,177
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ);

174
00:12:14,256 --> 00:12:17,802
كان بين آدم ونوح، عشرة قرون كلهم على الإسلام

175
00:12:18,564 --> 00:12:20,524
Rasool Ullah says in Al-Bukhari(البخاري);

176
00:12:20,889 --> 00:12:25,841
“Between Adam(آدَم) and Nuh(نوح), there were ten generations; all of them were Muslim.”

177
00:12:26,087 --> 00:12:30,659
Qarn(قرن) in Arabic means either century, a 100 years or generation.

178
00:12:31,746 --> 00:12:35,531
If it means ten centuries, that’s a Millenium, 1000 years.

179
00:12:35,984 --> 00:12:43,175
If it means 10 generations, it could be more than 1000 because we know that people used to live longer lives in those times.

180
00:12:43,712 --> 00:12:48,205
Between Adam(آدم) and Nuh(نوح), there were many generations, not 10, but ten of them were Muslim.

181
00:12:48,443 --> 00:12:53,435
So, out of the many generations between Adam(آدم) and Nuh(نوح), ten were Muslim,

182
00:12:54,141 --> 00:12:59,051
and then disbelief and Shirk(شرك‎) slowly started to creep in.

183
00:12:59,412 --> 00:13:00,666
How did it happen?

184
00:13:02,364 --> 00:13:06,383
Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) says, and this is the opinion of Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) mentioned in Al-Bukhari(البخاري),

185
00:13:06,542 --> 00:13:14,553
he says the descendants of Adam(آدم), they started slowly losing their religion and committing sins

186
00:13:15,236 --> 00:13:18,061
but they still believed in Tawheed (توحيد‎), the unity of Allah,

187
00:13:18,466 --> 00:13:22,314
but they were committing many sins and ignorance was spreading among them

188
00:13:23,743 --> 00:13:26,330
and the righteous men among them were few.

189
00:13:27,148 --> 00:13:29,462
Shaytan(شيطان) came to them and told them;

190
00:13:30,224 --> 00:13:38,339
“When these righteous men pass away, you will have no one to remind you about Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ and about Ibadah(عبادة),

191
00:13:38,609 --> 00:13:40,887
you will have nobody to give you Naseeha(نَصيحة) and advice.

192
00:13:41,895 --> 00:13:52,543
So how about when they pass away, you erect some statues in their memorial to remind you about Ibadah(عبادة)?”

193
00:13:52,868 --> 00:13:57,622
Because these righteous men used to remind the people, they used to give them naseeha(نصيحة) and advice;

194
00:13:57,924 --> 00:14:00,543
when they’re gonna pass away, who’s gonna give the people advice?

195
00:14:00,860 --> 00:14:05,198
So Shaytan(شيطان) told them: “How about when they pass away, you erect some statues

196
00:14:05,381 --> 00:14:11,022
so that whenever you would see the statue, you would remember good deeds and you would remember the righteous men?”

197
00:14:11,774 --> 00:14:17,837
They followed the advice of Shaytan(شيطان) thinking it was a good one, and they erected these idols.

198
00:14:19,107 --> 00:14:21,913
And then Shaytan(شيطان) left them alone. Shaytan(شيطان) is very, very patient.

199
00:14:22,655 --> 00:14:28,052
He left them alone for a while, until they forgot the reason why these idols were built.

200
00:14:28,338 --> 00:14:35,385
Generation after generation came and these statues were there, people forgot why these were built, why these were erected.

201
00:14:35,655 --> 00:14:37,565
Shaytan(شيطان) came to them and told them;

202
00:14:38,342 --> 00:14:40,899
“Why don’t you worship these statues?”

203
00:14:41,899 --> 00:14:43,549
And that is how Shirk(شرك‎) started.

204
00:14:44,565 --> 00:14:47,343
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ talks about these five idols;

205
00:14:48,025 --> 00:14:50,969
ود، سواع، يغوث، يعوق، نسر

206
00:14:51,080 --> 00:14:53,297
 five names of five idols.

207
00:14:53,853 --> 00:15:02,417
Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) says these were righteous men whom the people of Nuh(نوح) started worshipping their idols, their statues.

208
00:15:03,131 --> 00:15:04,988
So this is how Shirk(شرك‎) started.

209
00:15:06,053 --> 00:15:11,203
So Nuh(نوح) was the first Messenger of Allah to the people of the world,

210
00:15:11,799 --> 00:15:15,339
and that is mentioned in the authentic hadith(حديث‎) of Ash-Shafaʿah(الشفاعة‎),

211
00:15:15,593 --> 00:15:20,446
when the people on the Day of Judgement will go to Nuh(نوح), what will they tell him?

212
00:15:20,696 --> 00:15:22,639
أنت أول الرسل إلى أهل الأرض

213
00:15:22,956 --> 00:15:26,337
“You are the first Messenger of Allah to the people of the world.”

214
00:15:26,885 --> 00:15:30,960
So Sayyidina Nuh(سيدنا نوح) is the first Messenger to the people of the earth,

215
00:15:31,177 --> 00:15:33,677
and he is one of the five ‘Ulul-ʿAzm(أولو العزم).

216
00:15:33,907 --> 00:15:38,655
‘Ulul-ʿAzm(أولو العزم) are the greatest five of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎, Nuh(نوح) is one of them.

217
00:15:38,830 --> 00:15:45,163
The other 4 are Sayyidina(سيدنا) Muhammadﷺ, Ibrahim(إبراهيم‎), Musa(موسی), and ʿIsa(عيسى‎).

218
00:15:47,501 --> 00:15:54,301
Muhammad ﷺ, Ibrahim(إبراهيم‎), Nuh(نوح), Musa(موسی), and ʿIsa(عيسى‎), these 5 ‘Ulul-ʿAzmi Min Ar-Rusul(أولو العزم من الرسل).

219
00:15:56,484 --> 00:15:58,920
The greatest of them is Muhammad ﷺ.

220
00:15:59,849 --> 00:16:01,336
What was the message of Nuh(نوح)?

221
00:16:01,439 --> 00:16:02,637
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

222
00:16:02,677 --> 00:16:06,865
وَلَقَدْ أَرْسَلْنَا نُوحًا إِلَىٰ قَوْمِهِۦٓ إِنِّى لَكُمْ نَذِيرٌ مُّبِينٌ ۝

223
00:16:07,048 --> 00:16:09,071
 أَن لَّا تَعْبُدُوٓا۟ إِلَّا ٱللَّهَ

224
00:16:09,794 --> 00:16:10,789
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says:

225
00:16:10,829 --> 00:16:13,235
And indeed We sent Noah to his people

226
00:16:13,591 --> 00:16:20,244
and he said: “I have come to you as a plain warner that you worship none but Allah.

227
00:16:20,990 --> 00:16:24,851
This is the message that every Nabi(نبي‎) has presented to the world;

228
00:16:24,891 --> 00:16:29,368
Do not worship anyone but Allah - Tawheed(توحيد‎), the unity of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎.

229
00:16:29,574 --> 00:16:31,582
That is the message of every Nabi(نبي‎).

230
00:16:32,019 --> 00:16:32,696
And he tells them;

231
00:16:32,736 --> 00:16:35,423
أَنِ ٱعْبُدُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ وَٱتَّقُوهُ وَأَطِيعُونِ۝

232
00:16:35,931 --> 00:16:41,018
That you should worship Allah, be dutiful to Him, and obey me.

233
00:16:42,050 --> 00:16:46,657
So the Nabi(نبي‎) told them to “worship Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ and to have Taqwa(تقوى) and to obey me.”

234
00:16:46,848 --> 00:16:53,666
وَمَآ أَرْسَلْنَا مِن رَّسُولٍ إِلَّا لِيُطَاعَ بِإِذْنِ ٱللَّهِ

235
00:16:53,706 --> 00:16:56,689
Every Messenger that We sent, We sent him to be obeyed.

236
00:16:57,070 --> 00:16:59,914
The Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah don't just come and deliver a message and leave.

237
00:17:00,144 --> 00:17:03,105
They deliver the message and they tell the people that they have to obey them,

238
00:17:03,145 --> 00:17:06,898
and this is Tahkeem Ash-Shariʿah(تحكيم الشريعة‎) - this is the establishment of the Law of Allah.

239
00:17:07,406 --> 00:17:10,445
They came to be followed and to be obeyed.

240
00:17:12,239 --> 00:17:18,986
What were the methods of the Daʿwah(دعوة‎) of Nuh(نوح), what methods did he use, how did he perform his Daʿwah(دعوة‎)?

241
00:17:19,907 --> 00:17:21,169
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

242
00:17:21,280 --> 00:17:30,600
قَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّى دَعَوْتُ قَوْمِى لَيْلًا وَنَهَارًا۝

243
00:17:30,981 --> 00:17:36,094
He said: “O my Lord, verily, I have called my people night and day.”

244
00:17:37,007 --> 00:17:40,309
So he used to make Daʿwah(دعوة‎) to them in the night and day, and he said;

245
00:17:40,729 --> 00:17:47,625
ثُمَّ إِنِّى دَعَوْتُهُمْ جِهَارًا ۝

246
00:17:48,847 --> 00:18:00,686
 ثُمَّ إِنِّىٓ أَعْلَنتُ لَهُمْ وَأَسْرَرْتُ لَهُمْ إِسْرَارًا۝

247
00:18:01,496 --> 00:18:08,340
“Then verily, I called to them openly, then verily, I proclaimed to them in public and I have appealed to them in private.”

248
00:18:08,939 --> 00:18:13,147
So he used Jahar(جهر), which is announcing to everyone.

249
00:18:13,917 --> 00:18:17,790
And then he used Aʿlantu Lahum(أعلنت لهم), I would speak to them,

250
00:18:17,912 --> 00:18:20,705
and also, I would speak to them publicly and privately.

251
00:18:20,999 --> 00:18:25,613
So he used Daʿwah(دعوة‎) at night, he used Daʿwah(دعوة‎) at day, he used public and he used private.

252
00:18:26,066 --> 00:18:28,990
He varied his methods, he tried every way possible.

253
00:18:30,196 --> 00:18:35,426
So in our Daʿwah(دعوة‎), we should take advantage of every resource that we have.

254
00:18:35,855 --> 00:18:38,185
Everything, take advantage of everything;

255
00:18:38,701 --> 00:18:46,342
telephone, CDs, audio cassettes, Internet, speeches, Daʿwah(دعوة‎) on the individual level,

256
00:18:46,938 --> 00:18:54,818
visitations, through your Akhlaq(أخلاق‎), pamphlets, books, don't think that anything will not work.

257
00:18:54,863 --> 00:19:00,410
Use whatever you can because Sayyidina Nuh(سيدنا نوح) used whatever was possible to him.

258
00:19:00,823 --> 00:19:04,130
Any method, use it for the sake of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎.

259
00:19:05,979 --> 00:19:07,265
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

260
00:19:07,463 --> 00:19:16,566
فَلَمْ يَزِدْهُمْ دُعَآءِىٓ إِلَّا فِرَارًا۝

261
00:19:17,157 --> 00:19:22,420
But all my calling added nothing but to their flight from the truth.

262
00:19:22,793 --> 00:19:23,698
Allah Ho Akbar(الله أكبر).

263
00:19:24,357 --> 00:19:25,892
Nuh(نوح) is making Daʿwah(دعوة‎) to them,

264
00:19:25,947 --> 00:19:32,187
and the more Daʿwah(دعوة‎) he gives them, the further away they become, the further away they go.

265
00:19:32,782 --> 00:19:36,020
The more Daʿwah(دعوة‎) he makes, the more they fly away from him.

266
00:19:36,909 --> 00:19:44,772
The more Daʿwah(دعوة‎) he gives them, the worse the situation becomes, Difficult, Very difficult.

267
00:19:45,923 --> 00:19:48,057
And not only that, Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

268
00:19:48,192 --> 00:19:59,065
وَإِنِّى كُلَّمَا دَعَوْتُهُمْ لِتَغْفِرَ لَهُمْ جَعَلُوٓا۟ أَصَـٰبِعَهُمْ فِىٓ ءَاذَانِهِمْ وَٱسْتَغْشَوْا۟

269
00:19:59,311 --> 00:20:05,409
 وَٱسْتَغْشَوْا۟ ثِيَابَهُمْ وَأَصَرُّوا۟ وَٱسْتَكْبَرُوا۟ ٱسْتِكْبَارًا۝

270
00:20:05,647 --> 00:20:10,012
And verily, everytime I called unto them that You might forgive them,

271
00:20:10,171 --> 00:20:13,117
they thrust their fingers into their ears,

272
00:20:13,307 --> 00:20:19,870
covered themselves up with their garments, and persisted in their refusal, and magnified themselves in pride.

273
00:20:20,878 --> 00:20:25,326
He would give them Daʿwah(دعوة‎), he would be speaking to them, and they would put their fingers in their ears,

274
00:20:25,929 --> 00:20:30,199
or they would cover themselves with their clothes, and they would be arrogant and proud.

275
00:20:30,770 --> 00:20:32,405
If you are speaking to someone,

276
00:20:32,659 --> 00:20:38,386
and he starts putting his fingers in his ear, and he covers himself up, and he acts arrogantly towards you,

277
00:20:38,719 --> 00:20:40,539
will you be able to continue to talk to him?

278
00:20:41,507 --> 00:20:46,261
It’s very difficult, you would barely be able to do it for half an hour or an hour, and then you would be fed up and then you would leave

279
00:20:46,420 --> 00:20:47,930
and you would hate him for the rest of your life.

280
00:20:48,470 --> 00:20:51,430
Nuh(نوح) did this for 950 years.

281
00:20:53,287 --> 00:20:55,945
Nuh(نوح) was doing this for 950 years.

282
00:20:57,572 --> 00:21:03,389
950 years - he’s making Daʿwah(دعوة‎) night and day, publicly and privately,

283
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:07,585
and the more Daʿwah(دعوة‎) he gives, the worse the situation would become

284
00:21:08,061 --> 00:21:11,473
and the more animosity would become between him and his people,

285
00:21:11,823 --> 00:21:14,108
and the people are not listening to start with.

286
00:21:14,585 --> 00:21:18,146
He’s speaking to closed ears, but he had patience.

287
00:21:18,868 --> 00:21:21,233
He had patience for 950 years.

288
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:25,721
Sayyidina Nuh(سيدنا نوح) told his people about the value of istighfar(ٱستغفار‎).

289
00:21:25,975 --> 00:21:33,238
فَقُلْتُ ٱسْتَغْفِرُوا۟ رَبَّكُمْ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ غَفَّارًا۝

290
00:21:33,341 --> 00:21:38,175
I said to them: Ask forgiveness from your Lord; verily, He is Oft-Forgiving.

291
00:21:38,500 --> 00:21:41,306
And listen to the benefits of Istighfar(ٱستغفار‎).

292
00:21:41,433 --> 00:21:44,354
Nuh(نوح) is telling his people the benefits of Istighfar(ٱستغفار‎).

293
00:21:44,394 --> 00:21:46,418
If you make Istighfar(ٱستغفار‎), this is what will happen;

294
00:21:46,743 --> 00:21:51,596
يُرْسِلِ ٱلسَّمَآءَ عَلَيْكُم مِّدْرَارًا۝

295
00:21:51,715 --> 00:21:53,945
He will send rain to you in abundance.

296
00:21:54,255 --> 00:22:10,492
وَيُمْدِدْكُم بِأَمْوَٰلٍ وَبَنِينَ وَيَجْعَل لَّكُمْ جَنَّـٰتٍ وَيَجْعَل لَّكُمْ أَنْهَـٰرًا۝

297
00:22:11,198 --> 00:22:17,636
And give you increase in wealth and children, and bestow on you gardens, and bestow on you rivers.

298
00:22:18,406 --> 00:22:20,057
All of these are results of Istighfar(ٱستغفار‎).

299
00:22:20,565 --> 00:22:24,578
فٱستغفروا الله نستغفر الله العظيم ونتوب إليه

300
00:22:26,181 --> 00:22:29,656
And he also turned their attention to creation of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ around them

301
00:22:29,696 --> 00:22:34,791
because the creation of Allah is a mirror of the Attributes of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎.

302
00:22:35,299 --> 00:22:36,096
He told them;

303
00:22:36,330 --> 00:22:43,299
أَلَمْ تَرَوْا۟ كَيْفَ خَلَقَ ٱللَّهُ سَبْعَ سَمَـٰوَٰتٍ طِبَاقًا۝

304
00:22:43,410 --> 00:22:46,953
See you not how Allah has created seven heavens, one above the other?

305
00:22:47,096 --> 00:22:55,619
وَجَعَلَ ٱلْقَمَرَ فِيهِنَّ نُورًا وَجَعَلَ ٱلشَّمْسَ سِرَاجًا۝

306
00:22:55,865 --> 00:22:58,889
And has made the moon a light therein and made the sun a lamp?

307
00:22:59,397 --> 00:23:07,207
وَٱللَّهُ أَنۢبَتَكُم مِّنَ ٱلْأَرْضِ نَبَاتًا ۝

308
00:23:09,191 --> 00:23:17,750
 ثُمَّ يُعِيدُكُمْ فِيهَا وَيُخْرِجُكُمْ إِخْرَاجًا۝

309
00:23:18,417 --> 00:23:21,365
And Allah has brought you forth from the dust of the earth,

310
00:23:21,782 --> 00:23:26,734
afterwards He would return you into the earth and bring you forth again on the Day of Resurrection.

311
00:23:26,932 --> 00:23:31,242
وَٱللَّهُ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ ٱلْأَرْضَ بِسَاطًا ۝

312
00:23:31,393 --> 00:23:35,855
 لِّتَسْلُكُوا۟ مِنْهَا سُبُلًا فِجَاجًا۝

313
00:23:35,981 --> 00:23:41,505
And Allah has made for you the earth widespread that you may go about therein in broad roads.

314
00:23:42,315 --> 00:23:46,611
These are some of the Ayaat(آيات) of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ that he turned their attention to.

315
00:23:47,460 --> 00:23:54,531
When Nuh(نوح) was delivering this Daʿwah(دعوة‎), 950 years, only a few became Muslim,

316
00:23:55,563 --> 00:23:58,999
and these few tended to be from the weak and the poor.

317
00:23:59,555 --> 00:24:09,893
So, the leaders, the wealthy and the political leaders, influential men of the society, they came to Nuh(نوح) and they said;

318
00:24:10,139 --> 00:24:20,520
فَقَالَ ٱلْمَلَأُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ مِن قَوْمِهِۦ مَا نَرَىٰكَ إِلَّا بَشَرًا مِّثْلَنَا

319
00:24:21,099 --> 00:24:43,125
 إِلَّا بَشَرًا مِّثْلَنَا وَمَا نَرَىٰكَ ٱتَّبَعَكَ إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ هُمْ أَرَاذِلُنَا بَادِىَ ٱلرَّأْىِ وَمَا نَرَىٰ لَكُمْ عَلَيْنَا مِن فَضْلٍۭ بَلْ نَظُنُّكُمْ كَـٰذِبِينَ۝

320
00:24:43,332 --> 00:24:46,379
The chiefs of the disbelievers among his people said;

321
00:24:46,800 --> 00:24:52,644
We see you but a man like ourselves nor do we see any follow you but the meanest among us,

322
00:24:52,858 --> 00:24:54,993
and they too followed you without thinking.

323
00:24:56,112 --> 00:25:02,269
They told Nuh(نوح) that we don’t see any favour of you upon us.

324
00:25:02,333 --> 00:25:03,984
I mean, you’re not any better than us,

325
00:25:04,690 --> 00:25:06,633
and then they also told him that

326
00:25:07,109 --> 00:25:13,174
the people who followed you are the weakest and the meanest among us, and they followed you without thinking.

327
00:25:14,040 --> 00:25:14,841
Two things;

328
00:25:15,333 --> 00:25:18,368
The people who are following you are the weak and the poor;

329
00:25:18,781 --> 00:25:21,947
And the second thing, they followed you without thinking.

330
00:25:22,058 --> 00:25:23,416
 Let’s look at these two things;

331
00:25:25,249 --> 00:25:27,804
The followers of Nuh(نوح) were the weakest and the poorest;

332
00:25:29,423 --> 00:25:32,725
When Abu Sufyan (أبوسفيان) was on a business trip to Ar-Rum(الروم‎),

333
00:25:33,161 --> 00:25:36,202
he was visiting Ash-Sham(الشام) which was part of the Roman Empire at the time.

334
00:25:37,250 --> 00:25:41,202
Heracul(هرقل), the emperor of the Romans - Heraclius.

335
00:25:42,297 --> 00:25:44,669
He was in Ash-Sham(الشام) at the time

336
00:25:45,748 --> 00:25:52,091
and he heard about Muhammad ﷺ, so he demanded to meet one of his people.

337
00:25:52,131 --> 00:25:55,742
When he heard that there’s an Arab caravan that’s in town, he said;

338
00:25:55,901 --> 00:25:59,512
Go and see if any of them knows about Muhammad(محمد).

339
00:26:00,709 --> 00:26:07,261
So they went and brought these businessmen from Quraysh(قريش) to meet with the Roman emperor, Heracul(هرقل).

340
00:26:08,126 --> 00:26:11,324
So Heraclius asked this group;

341
00:26:11,673 --> 00:26:16,365
Who of you is the closest relative of Muhammadﷺ?

342
00:26:17,286 --> 00:26:18,696
So Abu Sufyan(أبوسفيان) said: “I am,”

343
00:26:18,736 --> 00:26:21,092
and he was the closest relative of him among the group.

344
00:26:23,163 --> 00:26:27,187
Heracul(هرقل) started asking Abu Sufyan(أبوسفيان) a few questions.

345
00:26:27,742 --> 00:26:32,236
One of these questions he said: “Who are the followers of this man?”

346
00:26:33,061 --> 00:26:38,560
Abu Sufyan(أبوسفيان) said: “His followers are the slaves, and the weak, and the poor, and the servant.”

347
00:26:40,012 --> 00:26:41,616
What did Heracul(هرقل) say?

348
00:26:42,282 --> 00:26:44,878
He said: “These are the followers of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).”

349
00:26:46,816 --> 00:26:48,889
These are the followers of the Messengers.

350
00:26:50,142 --> 00:26:53,512
These were the followers of ʿIsa(عيسى‎), these were the followers of Musa(موسی),

351
00:26:53,695 --> 00:26:56,667
these were the followers of Hud(هود‎), these were the followers of Salih(صالح)

352
00:26:57,072 --> 00:27:00,723
the people who follow the Ambiya(أنبياء) in the beginning are usually the weak and the poor.

353
00:27:00,802 --> 00:27:02,659
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ gives them this blessing.

354
00:27:03,779 --> 00:27:08,182
So, this point that the people of Nuh(نوح) are bringing is worthless.

355
00:27:09,317 --> 00:27:13,394
The second point is they followed you without thinking;

356
00:27:13,600 --> 00:27:17,181
They wanted them to study it, they wanted them to give it a second thought.

357
00:27:17,404 --> 00:27:25,327
This thing that they’re using as an accusation against Nuh(نوح) is actually a point of pride for those who believed,

358
00:27:25,565 --> 00:27:28,295
because what did Rasool Allah ﷺ praise Abu Bakr(أبو بكر) for?

359
00:27:29,057 --> 00:27:35,507
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: “Everyone I presented Islam to hesitated for a moment except Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

360
00:27:35,698 --> 00:27:40,898
As soon as I presented the Message to him, he accepted without giving it a second thought.

361
00:27:41,771 --> 00:27:45,412
When you receive truth, you shouldn’t give it a second thought, you shouldn’t sit on it for a while.

362
00:27:45,581 --> 00:27:48,883
When you receive truth, as long as it’s the truth, you immediately follow it.

363
00:27:49,026 --> 00:27:50,709
And that’s what these followers of Nuh(نوح) did.

364
00:27:50,828 --> 00:27:59,402
So these chiefs are accusing these followers with something that is actually a point of praise for them and honor.

365
00:28:00,211 --> 00:28:06,942
And you always find that they would accuse the Muslims today, with things that are, in reality, things that we should be proud of.

366
00:28:07,537 --> 00:28:08,727
Nuh(نوح) said;

367
00:28:09,005 --> 00:28:11,283
وَيَـٰقَوْمِ لَآ أَسْـَٔلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مَالًا

368
00:28:11,323 --> 00:28:15,154
And, O my people, I ask of you no wealth for it.

369
00:28:15,630 --> 00:28:21,740
It’s very important that the Daʿiyah(داعيه), the one who’s calling to the sake of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎,

370
00:28:21,973 --> 00:28:28,007
never want compensation, financial, material compensation for what he’s doing.

371
00:28:28,047 --> 00:28:33,606
It’s very important, the work should be done for the sake of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ alone.

372
00:28:34,011 --> 00:28:35,474
إِنْ أَجْرِىَ إِلَّا عَلَى ٱللَّهِ

373
00:28:35,514 --> 00:28:37,882
My reward is from none but Allah.

374
00:28:38,108 --> 00:28:38,696
And then he told them;

375
00:28:38,736 --> 00:28:40,918
وَمَآ أَنَا۠ بِطَارِدِ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓا۟

376
00:28:41,204 --> 00:28:44,189
I am not going to drive away those who have believed.

377
00:28:44,356 --> 00:28:45,539
These chiefs, they said;

378
00:28:45,689 --> 00:28:49,935
You have to kick out those weak and slaves, otherwise, we’re not going to listen to you.

379
00:28:50,451 --> 00:28:55,841
He said: I’m not gonna drive them out, these are the believers, these are the ones whom Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ honored with Islam.

380
00:28:57,195 --> 00:28:58,259
And then he told them;

381
00:28:58,735 --> 00:29:15,520
وَلَآ أَقُولُ لَكُمْ عِندِى خَزَآئِنُ ٱللَّهِ وَلَآ أَعْلَمُ ٱلْغَيْبَ وَلَآ أَقُولُ إِنِّى مَلَكٌ

382
00:29:15,893 --> 00:29:19,990
“And I do not say to you that with me are the treasures of Allah.”

383
00:29:21,013 --> 00:29:25,226
The Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ do not have to be wealthy for the people to follow them.

384
00:29:25,924 --> 00:29:30,909
Notice Nuh(نوح) is telling them about things which, usually, people look for, in their leaders.

385
00:29:31,738 --> 00:29:38,967
People want to see their leaders rich, we usually respect and honor the rich and the wealthy.

386
00:29:39,094 --> 00:29:44,591
If somebody’s poor, we don’t care about him and we wouldn’t follow him or we wouldn’t accept having him as a leader.

387
00:29:44,750 --> 00:29:46,242
Same thing that happened with Talut(طالوت‎).

388
00:29:46,520 --> 00:29:47,441
They said;

389
00:29:47,481 --> 00:29:48,785
وَلَمْ يُؤْتَ سَعَةً مِّنَ ٱلْمَالِ

390
00:29:48,825 --> 00:29:50,345
“He’s not rich.”

391
00:29:51,036 --> 00:29:51,915
Nuh(نوح) is telling them;

392
00:29:51,955 --> 00:29:56,884
“I don’t control the treasures of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ and I don’t have to be rich.”

393
00:29:57,662 --> 00:29:58,330
And he told them;

394
00:29:58,377 --> 00:29:59,155
وَلَآ أَعْلَمُ ٱلْغَيْبَ

395
00:29:59,195 --> 00:30:00,710
And I do not know the Unseen.

396
00:30:01,345 --> 00:30:04,564
We shouldn’t expect from the Ambiya(أنبياء) of Allah سبحانه وتعالى that they know Al-Ghaib(الغيب).

397
00:30:04,853 --> 00:30:09,044
He said: “I do not know the Unseen except what Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ would teach me.”

398
00:30:09,774 --> 00:30:11,419
And he told them: And I am not an angel.

399
00:30:11,523 --> 00:30:13,753
Because, always, whenever a Nabi(نبي‎) comes, they say;

400
00:30:14,332 --> 00:30:18,544
You should be an angel and you should be different, you shouldn’t be in human form.

401
00:30:18,584 --> 00:30:19,281
So he told them;

402
00:30:19,559 --> 00:30:20,765
وَلَآ أَقُولُ إِنِّى مَلَكٌ

403
00:30:20,845 --> 00:30:23,662
And I do not tell you that I am an angel.

404
00:30:23,876 --> 00:30:29,629
Nuh(نوح) is giving Daʿwah(دعوة‎) for 950 years and he did not get tired.

405
00:30:30,771 --> 00:30:37,184
He’s alone against all of the society, and he did not get tired and he never gave up.

406
00:30:37,676 --> 00:30:38,827
Who gave up?

407
00:30:39,120 --> 00:30:39,922
His people.

408
00:30:40,700 --> 00:30:43,498
His people gave up, it wasn’t Nuh(نوح).

409
00:30:44,165 --> 00:30:48,916
Nuh(نوح) persisted even though he was alone, and they were rejecting him,

410
00:30:49,450 --> 00:30:51,913
 but they are the ones who eventually gave up.

411
00:30:52,146 --> 00:31:02,375
قَالُوا۟ يَـٰنُوحُ قَدْ جَـٰدَلْتَنَا فَأَكْثَرْتَ جِدَٰلَنَا فَأْتِنَا بِمَا تَعِدُنَآ إِن كُنتَ

412
00:31:02,439 --> 00:31:06,796
إِن كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلصَّـٰدِقِينَ۝

413
00:31:06,843 --> 00:31:07,358
They gave up.

414
00:31:07,415 --> 00:31:12,843
They said: “O Nuh(نوح), you have disputed with us, and much have you prolonged this dispute with us.”

415
00:31:12,923 --> 00:31:14,232
This has been going for too long.

416
00:31:14,796 --> 00:31:18,225
Now bring upon us what you threaten us with, if you are truthful.

417
00:31:19,495 --> 00:31:20,411
They told Nuh(نوح);

418
00:31:20,594 --> 00:31:24,874
“You have been debating with us and this debate has been prolonged.

419
00:31:24,954 --> 00:31:26,267
It’s taking too long;

420
00:31:26,569 --> 00:31:29,815
can you please end it and bring the punishment of Allah that you said?

421
00:31:30,378 --> 00:31:30,893
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله).

422
00:31:31,005 --> 00:31:33,942
Look at the Sabr(صبر) of the Nabi(نبي‎), he never gave up,

423
00:31:34,148 --> 00:31:39,204
and the whole society, one against the whole, and they lost.

424
00:31:40,413 --> 00:31:44,960
One person, alone, was able to stand against the whole society,

425
00:31:45,333 --> 00:31:47,895
and in the end, they are the ones who blinked first.

426
00:31:48,785 --> 00:31:50,864
They said: “You bring the punishment if you can.”

427
00:31:51,880 --> 00:31:53,968
قَدْ جَـٰدَلْتَنَا فَأَكْثَرْتَ جِدَٰلَنَا

428
00:31:54,008 --> 00:31:54,698
We’re tired.

429
00:31:55,706 --> 00:31:56,899
And they threatened him;

430
00:31:56,979 --> 00:32:05,010
قَالُوا۟ لَئِن لَّمْ تَنتَهِ يَـٰنُوحُ لَتَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلْمَرْجُومِينَ۝

431
00:32:05,035 --> 00:32:10,901
They said: If you cease not, if you don’t stop,“O Nuh(نوح), you will surely be among those stoned to death.

432
00:32:10,996 --> 00:32:12,266
We’re gonna stone you to death.

433
00:32:12,813 --> 00:32:17,702
Now, Nuh(نوح) started making Duʿa(دعاء) against them

434
00:32:18,636 --> 00:32:23,636
because they reached a level where they’re threatening him to take away his life,

435
00:32:24,159 --> 00:32:27,182
they don’t want to believe anymore, they want to end it.

436
00:32:27,695 --> 00:32:30,037
So Nuh(نوح) told Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎;

437
00:32:30,124 --> 00:32:48,382
قَالَ نُوحٌ رَّبِّ إِنَّهُمْ عَصَوْنِى وَٱتَّبَعُوا۟ مَن لَّمْ يَزِدْهُ مَالُهُۥ وَوَلَدُهُۥٓ إِلَّا خَسَارًا۝

438
00:32:48,715 --> 00:32:54,520
My Lord, they have disobeyed me and followed one whose wealth and children gave him no increase but loss.

439
00:32:54,655 --> 00:32:57,846
 They followed the wealthy and they followed the strong families.

440
00:32:58,251 --> 00:33:00,372
These are the ones who they followed, “they didn’t follow me.”

441
00:33:00,832 --> 00:33:01,864
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ said;

442
00:33:01,904 --> 00:33:10,145
وَأُوحِىَ إِلَىٰ نُوحٍ أَنَّهُۥ لَن يُؤْمِنَ مِن قَوْمِكَ إِلَّا مَن قَدْ ءَامَنَ

443
00:33:10,192 --> 00:33:11,471
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

444
00:33:11,774 --> 00:33:18,124
And it was inspired to Nuh(نوح): “None of your people will believe except those who have already believed.

445
00:33:18,295 --> 00:33:21,089
So, be not sad because of what they used to do.

446
00:33:21,390 --> 00:33:23,835
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ told Nuh(نوح): No one else will believe.

447
00:33:24,525 --> 00:33:27,428
Nuh(نوح) now started making Duʿa(دعاء) to Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎

448
00:33:27,500 --> 00:33:35,863
when he saw that we reached to the end, there is no further dialogue between us, the communication is cut.

449
00:33:36,127 --> 00:33:40,443
وَلَقَدْ نَادَىٰنَا نُوحٌ فَلَنِعْمَ ٱلْمُجِيبُونَ۝

450
00:33:40,483 --> 00:33:45,278
And indeed, Nuh invoked Us, and We are the best of those who answer.

451
00:33:46,079 --> 00:33:48,498
Nuh(نوح) made a Duʿa(دعاء) and We will answer it.

452
00:33:48,897 --> 00:33:49,738
Nuh(نوح) said;

453
00:33:50,365 --> 00:33:57,768
وَقَالَ نُوحٌ رَّبِّ لَا تَذَرْ عَلَى ٱلْأَرْضِ مِنَ ٱلْكَـٰفِرِينَ دَيَّارًا ۝

454
00:33:58,022 --> 00:34:09,229
إِنَّكَ إِن تَذَرْهُمْ يُضِلُّوا۟ عِبَادَكَ وَلَا يَلِدُوٓا۟ إِلَّا فَاجِرًا كَفَّارًا۝

455
00:34:09,666 --> 00:34:10,825
Nuh(نوح) made his Duʿa(دعاء).

456
00:34:11,340 --> 00:34:16,642
After 950 years of patience, he finally made a Duʿa(دعاء) against his people and he said;

457
00:34:16,951 --> 00:34:21,261
O Allah, leave none of the non-believers on the face of the earth.

458
00:34:21,753 --> 00:34:23,197
Destroy them all.

459
00:34:23,474 --> 00:34:24,120
Why?

460
00:34:24,388 --> 00:34:28,708
It's not because of a personal problem between Nuh(نوح) and them, no.

461
00:34:28,758 --> 00:34:29,879
Nuh(نوح) said;

462
00:34:30,280 --> 00:34:38,669
If You leave them, they will mislead Your servants and they will beget none but wicked disbelievers.

463
00:34:39,946 --> 00:34:42,104
Nuh(نوح) said: “O Allah, destroy them.” Why?

464
00:34:42,220 --> 00:34:48,290
Because “if You leave them, they are going to deliver this disbelief to their children and they’re gonna insist on it,

465
00:34:48,564 --> 00:34:52,955
and then they are going to corrupt the believers, so destroy them all.

466
00:34:53,157 --> 00:34:56,906
And the Duʿa(دعاء) was received by Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎.

467
00:34:57,901 --> 00:35:03,030
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ instructed Nuh (نوح) to build the ark - the ship.

468
00:35:03,261 --> 00:35:07,061
وَٱصْنَعِ ٱلْفُلْكَ بِأَعْيُنِنَا وَوَحْيِنَا

469
00:35:07,101 --> 00:35:12,184
And construct the ship under Our eyes and with Our inspiration.

470
00:35:12,610 --> 00:35:15,511
So, Nuh(نوح) started constructing the ark.

471
00:35:16,218 --> 00:35:19,093
وَلَا تُخَـٰطِبْنِى فِى ٱلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوٓا۟ ۚ إِنَّهُم مُّغْرَقُونَ۝

472
00:35:19,338 --> 00:35:22,260
And address Me not on behalf of those who did wrong.

473
00:35:22,361 --> 00:35:23,890
They are surely to be drowned.

474
00:35:23,999 --> 00:35:25,964
So, he started building the ark.

475
00:35:26,397 --> 00:35:27,277
وَيَصْنَعُ ٱلْفُلْكَ

476
00:35:27,775 --> 00:35:35,953
And as he was constructing the ship, whenever the chiefs of his people would pass by, they would make fun of him.

477
00:35:36,033 --> 00:35:37,081
They mocked at him.

478
00:35:37,860 --> 00:35:38,654
تَسْخَرُونَ

479
00:35:39,036 --> 00:35:40,098
they would make fun of him.

480
00:35:40,408 --> 00:35:42,789
Nuh(نوح), are you crazy, did you lose your mind?

481
00:35:43,215 --> 00:35:45,134
You're building a ship and there's no sea?

482
00:35:45,473 --> 00:35:49,172
Nuh(نوح) is building an ark on top of this hill,

483
00:35:49,497 --> 00:35:54,987
and there's no sea and ocean and there's no river, there’s nothing, and Nuh(نوح) is building a ship.

484
00:35:55,413 --> 00:35:56,724
So, they would come next to him

485
00:35:56,753 --> 00:36:03,517
because, Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), the people of Duniya(دنيا‎) can only see what is in front of their eyes,

486
00:36:04,239 --> 00:36:08,554
they cannot understand that Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ is able to do.

487
00:36:08,594 --> 00:36:09,871
إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيرٌ۝

488
00:36:10,112 --> 00:36:13,721
They are limited with this narrow vision of the material world.

489
00:36:14,211 --> 00:36:16,722
There's no sea, there's no river, there's no ocean, what’re you doing?

490
00:36:17,040 --> 00:36:18,360
And they would make fun of Nuh(نوح).

491
00:36:19,031 --> 00:36:19,943
Nuh(نوح) told them;

492
00:36:20,238 --> 00:36:32,967
قَالَ إِن تَسْخَرُوا۟ مِنَّا فَإِنَّا نَسْخَرُ مِنكُمْ كَمَا تَسْخَرُونَ۝

493
00:36:33,176 --> 00:36:38,169
If you mock at us, so do we mock at you likewise for your mocking.

494
00:36:38,515 --> 00:36:44,960
فَسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُونَ مَن يَأْتِيهِ عَذَابٌ يُخْزِيهِ

495
00:36:45,053 --> 00:36:50,344
وَيَحِلُّ عَلَيْهِ عَذَابٌ مُّقِيمٌ۝

496
00:36:50,384 --> 00:36:58,619
And you will know who it is on whom will come a torment that will cover him with disgrace and on whom will fall a lasting torment.

497
00:36:59,340 --> 00:37:06,198
حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا جَآءَ أَمْرُنَا

498
00:37:06,238 --> 00:37:09,248
So it was, till then came our command.

499
00:37:09,559 --> 00:37:10,937
وَفَارَ ٱلتَّنُّورُ

500
00:37:11,225 --> 00:37:19,337
The springs of the earth started gushing with water and rain started falling from the sky.

501
00:37:19,525 --> 00:37:26,045
قُلْنَا ٱحْمِلْ فِيهَا مِن كُلٍّ زَوْجَيْنِ ٱثْنَيْنِ وَأَهْلَكَ

502
00:37:26,114 --> 00:37:32,258
 وَأَهْلَكَ إِلَّا مَن سَبَقَ عَلَيْهِ ٱلْقَوْلُ

503
00:37:32,285 --> 00:37:37,537
  إِلَّا مَن سَبَقَ عَلَيْهِ ٱلْقَوْلُ وَمَنْ ءَامَنَ ۚ

504
00:37:37,577 --> 00:37:43,987
 وَمَآ ءَامَنَ مَعَهُۥٓ إِلَّا قَلِيلٌ۝

505
00:37:44,027 --> 00:37:45,524
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

506
00:37:45,783 --> 00:37:50,526
So it was, till then there came our command and the oven gushed forth.

507
00:37:51,027 --> 00:37:55,499
We said: Embark therein of each kind two, male and female,

508
00:37:55,550 --> 00:38:02,944
and your family, except him against whom the word has already gone forth and those who believed with you.

509
00:38:03,097 --> 00:38:05,084
And only a few have believed with Nuh(نوح).

510
00:38:05,632 --> 00:38:10,784
When the water started coming out from the earth and rain falling from the sky,

511
00:38:11,058 --> 00:38:17,599
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ instructed Nuh(نوح) to go in the ark and to take with him the believers and to take with him his family

512
00:38:17,967 --> 00:38:22,183
and to carry a pair, male and female, of every animal.

513
00:38:22,746 --> 00:38:30,202
The number of the believers with Nuh(نوح) goes from 7 till 80.

514
00:38:30,267 --> 00:38:32,215
80 is the maximum number narrated.

515
00:38:33,867 --> 00:38:37,548
That's the maximum, but then there’s 7 and there's 8 and there’s different numbers.

516
00:38:37,822 --> 00:38:43,509
Maximum is 80; after 950 years of work, the fruit is 80.

517
00:38:45,147 --> 00:38:49,939
Brothers and sisters, sometimes, when we listen to this, reflect.

518
00:38:51,302 --> 00:38:56,598
We receive encouragement in our work when we see the fruits of it.

519
00:38:57,892 --> 00:39:02,199
When you are studying and you’re receiving good grades, that encourages you to study.

520
00:39:03,426 --> 00:39:07,744
When you are doing business and your business is flourishing, it encourages you to do business.

521
00:39:09,014 --> 00:39:13,099
But when you see that your effort is put in something that is not improving,

522
00:39:14,415 --> 00:39:20,810
and the more work you do the worse the situation becomes, it is very, very difficult, extremely difficult, to go on.

523
00:39:22,210 --> 00:39:25,408
Nuh(نوح), for 950 years, is not seeing anything happening in front of his eyes.

524
00:39:25,519 --> 00:39:26,584
Nobody is believing.

525
00:39:27,731 --> 00:39:30,924
But because he had trust that Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ is the One who rewards,

526
00:39:31,194 --> 00:39:32,997
he's not waiting for reward in Duniya(دنيا‎).

527
00:39:33,106 --> 00:39:38,957
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ is the One who gives the Ajr(أجر); he kept on and persisted on doing this for 950 years.

528
00:39:40,400 --> 00:39:44,454
That is the Yaqeen(یقین‎) and Tawakkul(توكل‎) and Eeman(إيمان) in Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎.

529
00:39:46,141 --> 00:39:48,281
When he went on the ark, what did he say?

530
00:39:48,321 --> 00:39:49,591
بسم الله‎

531
00:39:50,203 --> 00:39:52,355
Whenever we start something, we say Bismillah(بسم الله‎).

532
00:39:52,395 --> 00:39:54,113
وَقَالَ ٱرْكَبُوا۟ فِيهَا بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ

533
00:39:54,776 --> 00:39:57,909
And he said: Embark therein; in the name of Allah.

534
00:39:58,102 --> 00:39:59,676
So we start everything in the name of Allah;

535
00:39:59,716 --> 00:40:01,069
we start Salah(صلاة) in the name of Allah,

536
00:40:01,170 --> 00:40:02,310
we start eating in the name of Allah,

537
00:40:02,476 --> 00:40:04,234
when we go to bed, in the name of Allah,

538
00:40:04,366 --> 00:40:06,582
when we go in our cars, in the name of Allah.

539
00:40:06,717 --> 00:40:09,019
We start everything in the name of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎.

540
00:40:09,040 --> 00:40:09,769
بسم الله‎

541
00:40:10,765 --> 00:40:15,630
Allah is saying that this ark is on these waves, and what description was given to the waves?

542
00:40:15,792 --> 00:40:19,355
وَهِىَ تَجْرِى بِهِمْ فِى مَوْجٍ كَٱلْجِبَالِ

543
00:40:20,143 --> 00:40:26,933
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says: [So it] the ship [sailed with them amidst waves like mountains.]

544
00:40:27,626 --> 00:40:29,877
We’re talking here about waves like mountains.

545
00:40:31,262 --> 00:40:33,961
What is a mountain, 1000 feet, 2000 feet?

546
00:40:34,415 --> 00:40:38,198
Imagine waves 1000 feet high or 2000 feet high.

547
00:40:38,524 --> 00:40:43,502
Not even the biggest US aircraft carrier can sustain these waves.

548
00:40:44,109 --> 00:40:49,265
So, it's not the ark, it's not this ship that Nuh(نوح) built that gave them safety.

549
00:40:49,893 --> 00:40:57,487
It is not this ark that saved them from these waves, these are only the Asbab(اسباب).

550
00:40:57,527 --> 00:41:01,343
This is the part that Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ told Nuh(نوح) to do.

551
00:41:01,554 --> 00:41:07,563
Otherwise, that ark would be like a matchbox in these waves, it would not be able to survive at all.

552
00:41:08,361 --> 00:41:10,749
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ wants Nuh(نوح) to do his part;

553
00:41:11,334 --> 00:41:14,299
just build the ark, but it's not the ark that will do you anything.

554
00:41:15,057 --> 00:41:20,437
It is the Will of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ and the care of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ that will take care of you and save you.

555
00:41:21,527 --> 00:41:25,352
So Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ told Nuh(نوح) to build the ark because you have to do your part.

556
00:41:26,340 --> 00:41:29,255
You have to do your part, you have to take the first step.

557
00:41:30,049 --> 00:41:32,193
إن مشيت إلي، هرولت إليك

558
00:41:32,233 --> 00:41:35,858
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says: If you walk towards Me, I will run towards you.

559
00:41:36,537 --> 00:41:37,809
You have to take the first step.

560
00:41:38,110 --> 00:41:40,324
وَٱلَّذِينَ ٱهْتَدَوْاْ زَادَهُمْ هُدًى

561
00:41:40,497 --> 00:41:45,136
The ones who seek guidance, you seek it, you look for it - Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ will guide them.

562
00:41:46,716 --> 00:41:51,952
The victory of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ comes after you do your part, and that is what Nuh(نوح) is able to do, he build an ark,

563
00:41:53,071 --> 00:41:55,084
but the rest is on Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎.

564
00:41:56,195 --> 00:42:02,428
The waves picked up this ark and Nuh(نوح) is seeing his son in front of his eyes.

565
00:42:02,746 --> 00:42:04,602
He's telling his son: “Come and join us.”

566
00:42:04,847 --> 00:42:11,095
وَنَادَىٰ نُوحٌ ٱبْنَهُۥ وَكَانَ فِى مَعْزِلٍ يَـٰبُنَىَّ ٱرْكَب مَّعَنَا

567
00:42:11,454 --> 00:42:16,382
 يَـٰبُنَىَّ ٱرْكَب مَّعَنَا وَلَا تَكُن مَّعَ ٱلْكَـٰفِرِينَ۝

568
00:42:16,839 --> 00:42:20,411
O my son, embark with us and don’t be with the non-believers.

569
00:42:20,742 --> 00:42:26,912
His son, thinking in the terms of this material world, said;

570
00:42:27,229 --> 00:42:34,315
قَالَ سَـَٔاوِىٓ إِلَىٰ جَبَلٍ يَعْصِمُنِى مِنَ ٱلْمَآءِ

571
00:42:34,438 --> 00:42:38,731
I will seek refuge in a mountain that will save me from this water.

572
00:42:39,445 --> 00:42:41,359
He thought that a mountain will save him.

573
00:42:42,160 --> 00:42:45,357
I mean, rain cannot cover mountains, we never saw that in our life.

574
00:42:45,898 --> 00:42:49,345
Thinking in terms of the material world, he thought that this mountain will save him.

575
00:42:49,496 --> 00:42:50,492
His father told him;

576
00:42:50,607 --> 00:42:56,321
قَالَ لَا عَاصِمَ ٱلْيَوْمَ مِنْ أَمْرِ ٱللَّهِ إِلَّا مَن رَّحِمَ

577
00:42:56,660 --> 00:43:00,167
There's nothing that can save you on this day except the mercy of Allah.

578
00:43:01,624 --> 00:43:02,396
He refused.

579
00:43:03,613 --> 00:43:04,587
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

580
00:43:04,627 --> 00:43:07,553
وَحَالَ بَيْنَهُمَا ٱلْمَوْجُ فَكَانَ مِنَ ٱلْمُغْرَقِينَ۝

581
00:43:08,187 --> 00:43:11,919
Waves separated between them, and he drowned.

582
00:43:12,798 --> 00:43:20,715
Imagine standing and you see your son, in front of your eyes, and the waves are separating between you and him slowly.

583
00:43:21,618 --> 00:43:24,418
And in front of your eyes, you know that that's the end of your son.

584
00:43:24,771 --> 00:43:27,326
It's the end of it…what a difficult situation,

585
00:43:28,120 --> 00:43:29,167
سبحان الله العظيم

586
00:43:29,830 --> 00:43:40,405
وَقِيلَ يَـٰٓأَرْضُ ٱبْلَعِى مَآءَكِ وَيَـٰسَمَآءُ أَقْلِعِى

587
00:43:40,542 --> 00:43:46,052
Rain stopped from the sky and Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ instructed, commanded the earth to swallow all of the water.

588
00:43:46,406 --> 00:43:47,463
وَٱسْتَوَتْ عَلَى ٱلْجُودِىِّ

589
00:43:47,510 --> 00:43:52,066
So this ark landed on the mountain called Al-Judi(ٱلجودى), Judi(جودي) mountain.

590
00:43:52,531 --> 00:43:55,526
It is said that it’s in present-day Kurdistan.

591
00:43:55,670 --> 00:43:58,548
That’s where they say the mountain is, that's where it landed.

592
00:43:59,060 --> 00:44:04,985
And when everything settled, Nuh(نوح) wanted to ask Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ about something.

593
00:44:05,718 --> 00:44:06,504
Nuh(نوح) said;

594
00:44:07,074 --> 00:44:15,786
وَنَادَىٰ نُوحٌ رَّبَّهُۥ فَقَالَ رَبِّ إِنَّ ٱبْنِى مِنْ أَهْلِى وَإِنَّ وَعْدَكَ ٱلْحَقُّ

595
00:44:15,898 --> 00:44:23,096
 وَإِنَّ وَعْدَكَ ٱلْحَقُّ وَأَنتَ أَحْكَمُ ٱلْحَـٰكِمِينَ۝

596
00:44:23,277 --> 00:44:25,254
And Nuh(نوح) called upon his Lord and said;

597
00:44:25,294 --> 00:44:34,248
O my Lord, verily my son is of my family, and certainly Your promise is true, and You are the Most Just of the judges.

598
00:44:35,093 --> 00:44:40,034
Allah has promised Nuh(نوح) that you will be saved with your family.

599
00:44:41,801 --> 00:44:44,456
So Nuh(نوح) is asking Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ and saying;

600
00:44:44,565 --> 00:44:49,383
O Allah, didn't You tell me that all of my family will be saved?

601
00:44:49,888 --> 00:44:53,904
And my son is from my family and Your promise is true.

602
00:44:53,944 --> 00:44:56,220
Nuh(نوح) is saying that I don't have any doubts in Your promise.

603
00:44:56,260 --> 00:44:59,834
This is not doubt, he just wants to know, understand.

604
00:45:00,736 --> 00:45:02,621
إِنَّ وَعْدَكَ ٱلْحَقُّ وَأَنتَ أَحْكَمُ ٱلْحَـٰكِمِينَ۝

605
00:45:02,692 --> 00:45:07,625
Your promise is true, and You are the Most Wise and the Just of the judges.

606
00:45:08,260 --> 00:45:11,110
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ taught Nuh(نوح) a lesson.

607
00:45:11,976 --> 00:45:18,766
We use words to mean some things, but Islam comes and gives them a new definition.

608
00:45:19,185 --> 00:45:23,101
Salah(صلاة), for example, had the definition of supplication before Islam.

609
00:45:23,141 --> 00:45:27,469
But then Islam gave it Maʿana Istilahi(معنى اصطلاحي), it gave it the meaning of the Salah(صلاة).

610
00:45:28,550 --> 00:45:36,734
The meaning of happiness, for example we think of happiness in certain way but Islam defined happiness in a different way.

611
00:45:37,626 --> 00:45:40,202
Family has a definition among us.

612
00:45:40,440 --> 00:45:41,075
What is it?

613
00:45:41,234 --> 00:45:42,480
Your blood relatives.

614
00:45:42,797 --> 00:45:45,339
The blood relation, that’s what we call family.

615
00:45:45,670 --> 00:45:49,555
And Nuh(نوح) is considering his son to be part of his family because he’s his blood son.

616
00:45:50,194 --> 00:45:55,337
But Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ is now going to teach Nuh(نوح) the true meaning of family.

617
00:45:55,678 --> 00:45:57,653
So Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ is telling Nuh(نوح),

618
00:45:57,875 --> 00:46:12,182
قَالَ يَـٰنُوحُ إِنَّهُۥ لَيْسَ مِنْ أَهْلِكَ ۖ إِنَّهُۥ عَمَلٌ غَيْرُ صَـٰلِحٍ ۖ فَلَا تَسْـَٔلْنِ مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ بِهِۦ عِلْمٌ ۖ

619
00:46:12,788 --> 00:46:27,680
فَلَا تَسْـَٔلْنِ مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ بِهِۦ عِلْمٌ ۖ إِنِّىٓ أَعِظُكَ أَن تَكُونَ مِنَ ٱلْجَـٰهِلِينَ۝

620
00:46:28,458 --> 00:46:29,990
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ said;

621
00:46:30,244 --> 00:46:37,772
O Nuh(نوح), surely he is not of your family; verily, his work is unrighteous.

622
00:46:39,367 --> 00:46:44,126
Because his work is unrighteous, he is not part of your family anymore.

623
00:46:44,745 --> 00:46:49,364
He is your family if he is a righteous Muslim.

624
00:46:50,301 --> 00:46:52,903
Nuh(نوح) understood, and he said;

625
00:46:53,062 --> 00:46:59,933
قَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّىٓ أَعُوذُ بِكَ أَنْ أَسْـَٔلَكَ مَا لَيْسَ لِى بِهِۦ عِلْمٌ

626
00:46:59,973 --> 00:47:04,568
O my Lord, I seek refuge with You from asking You that of which I have no knowledge.

627
00:47:04,774 --> 00:47:05,552
And then he made a Duʿa(دعاء);

628
00:47:05,592 --> 00:47:09,091
وَإِلَّا تَغْفِرْ لِى وَتَرْحَمْنِىٓ أَكُن مِّنَ ٱلْخَـٰسِرِينَ۝

629
00:47:09,259 --> 00:47:13,990
And unless You forgive me and have mercy on me, I would indeed be one of the losers.

630
00:47:14,742 --> 00:47:21,797
The story of Nuh(نوح) has been mentioned in many Surah(سورة‎) of Qur'an, but the longest version is in Surat Hud(هود‎ سورة‎).

631
00:47:21,996 --> 00:47:26,480
It starts with Ayah(آية‎) 25 and goes up till ayah (آية‎) 49.

632
00:47:27,154 --> 00:47:33,977
After this long version of story of Nuh(نوح) that is revealed to Rasool Allah ﷺ from Ayah(آية‎) Verse 25 till 48,

633
00:47:35,240 --> 00:47:38,468
Ayah(آية‎) Verse 49 is telling Rasool Allah ﷺ,

634
00:47:39,595 --> 00:47:59,810
تِلْكَ مِنْ أَنۢبَآءِ ٱلْغَيْبِ نُوحِيهَآ إِلَيْكَ ۖ مَا كُنتَ تَعْلَمُهَآ أَنتَ وَلَا قَوْمُكَ مِن قَبْلِ هَـٰذَا

635
00:48:00,032 --> 00:48:06,118
This is of the news of the Unseen which We reveal unto you.

636
00:48:06,301 --> 00:48:09,904
Neither you nor your people knew them before this.

637
00:48:10,205 --> 00:48:14,282
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ is telling Muhammad ﷺ after this long story;

638
00:48:15,512 --> 00:48:18,575
This is the closure, this is the conclusion of the story of Nuh(نوح).

639
00:48:19,401 --> 00:48:27,786
O Muhammad(محمد), this is the true news of Nuh(نوح) that is revealed to you.

640
00:48:28,103 --> 00:48:31,615
Neither you nor your people knew it before.

641
00:48:32,584 --> 00:48:33,814
So what’s the lesson?

642
00:48:34,401 --> 00:48:36,312
All of this in leading to the next word.

643
00:48:36,384 --> 00:48:37,503
What is the lesson?

644
00:48:37,971 --> 00:48:39,348
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ is saying;

645
00:48:39,388 --> 00:48:40,447
 فَٱصْبِرْ

646
00:48:40,995 --> 00:48:42,327
Be patient.

647
00:48:42,871 --> 00:48:49,078
All of the story of Nuh(نوح), from Ayah(آية‎) Verse 25 till 48, is leading to this Ibrah(عبرة), to this meaning.

648
00:48:49,340 --> 00:48:55,445
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ is closing this story of Nuh(نوح), telling Rasool Allah ﷺ look at the story of Nuh(نوح);

649
00:48:55,913 --> 00:49:01,997
950 years of patience, of making Daʿwah(دعوة‎) to his people, he never gave up,

650
00:49:02,202 --> 00:49:05,517
he persisted and he made Daʿwah(دعوة‎) to them in the night and the day,

651
00:49:05,612 --> 00:49:07,818
he made Daʿwah(دعوة‎) to them publicly and privately,

652
00:49:07,969 --> 00:49:09,756
he made Daʿwah(دعوة‎) to them and he was alone,

653
00:49:09,930 --> 00:49:12,549
he made Daʿwah(دعوة‎) to them and they were not listening to him.

654
00:49:12,803 --> 00:49:14,033
What is the lesson to learn?

655
00:49:14,232 --> 00:49:15,165
 فَٱصْبِرْ

656
00:49:15,359 --> 00:49:15,964
Be patient.

657
00:49:16,012 --> 00:49:17,900
إِنَّ ٱلْعَـٰقِبَةَ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ۝

658
00:49:18,020 --> 00:49:22,681
The end result, the winners in the end, are going to be who?

659
00:49:22,808 --> 00:49:23,966
The ones who have Taqwa(تقوى).

660
00:49:24,482 --> 00:49:25,451
This is the lesson.

661
00:49:25,617 --> 00:49:29,301
فَٱصْبِرْ ۖ إِنَّ ٱلْعَـٰقِبَةَ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ۝

662
00:49:29,690 --> 00:49:35,507
Be patient and remember that in the end, the ones who will win are the believers.

663
00:49:36,531 --> 00:49:40,577
Nuh(نوح) did win, but he won after 950 years,

664
00:49:43,070 --> 00:49:45,686
and he couldn't have won if he didn't have patience.

665
00:49:46,551 --> 00:49:54,257
So the road is long and it needs a lot of energy, and that energy is Sabr(صبر).

666
00:49:54,757 --> 00:49:59,327
If you don't have it, you're gonna fall in the middle of the way, you’re not gonna be able to complete it.

667
00:49:59,836 --> 00:50:02,495
So we ask Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ to give us the patience that we need.

668
00:50:03,090 --> 00:50:04,828
اللهم اجعلنا من الصابرين

669
00:50:05,765 --> 00:50:09,426
You have the story of Sayyidina Hud(سيدنا هود‎).

670
00:50:11,029 --> 00:50:16,085
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ has sent Hud(هود‎) to the people of ʿAd(عاد).

671
00:50:17,108 --> 00:50:23,761
We wouldn't have known where ʿAd(عاد) lived if it wasn't mentioned in Qur'an.

672
00:50:25,221 --> 00:50:30,535
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says that the people of ʿAd(عاد) lived in Al-Ahqaf(الأحقاف‎),

673
00:50:31,519 --> 00:50:34,035
and that is mentioned in Surat Al-Ahqaf(الأحقاف‎ سورة‎).

674
00:50:34,996 --> 00:50:37,467
Al-Ahqaf(الأحقاف‎) means sand dunes.

675
00:50:37,734 --> 00:50:42,083
So, it's a desert area right now, it wasn't that case before.

676
00:50:42,805 --> 00:50:48,289
And this is in Yemen, and they lived in the area of Hadramaut(حضرموت‎).

677
00:50:49,313 --> 00:50:54,369
The people of ʿAd(عاد) - Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ described them in Qur'an.

678
00:50:56,813 --> 00:50:59,297
The people of ʿAd(عاد) used to worship idols.

679
00:51:01,416 --> 00:51:06,142
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ described these people, and their description is amazing.

680
00:51:06,523 --> 00:51:09,150
What Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ has given them is amazing.

681
00:51:10,475 --> 00:51:14,293
As individuals, Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

682
00:51:14,333 --> 00:51:20,324
وَزَادَكُمْ فِى ٱلْخَلْقِ بَصْۜطَةً

683
00:51:20,602 --> 00:51:23,769
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ has increased you amply in stature.

684
00:51:25,182 --> 00:51:32,756
So they were huge, tall, and very strong and well-built, powerful, as individuals very strong.

685
00:51:34,574 --> 00:51:38,161
And as a society and a nation and a civilization,

686
00:51:38,479 --> 00:51:41,832
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ told them or described them in Qur'an

687
00:51:41,935 --> 00:51:44,697
and these are Ayaat(آيات) in Qur'an,

688
00:51:44,777 --> 00:51:48,642
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ is mentioning what their Nabi Hud(هود‎ نبي‎) was telling them;

689
00:51:49,134 --> 00:51:55,436
وَٱتَّقُوا ٱلَّذِى أَمَدَّكُم بِمَا تَعْلَمُونَ۝

690
00:51:55,476 --> 00:52:00,764
And keep your duty to Him. Fear Him Who has aided you with all things that you know.

691
00:52:01,261 --> 00:52:06,392
أَمَدَّكُم بِأَنْعَـٰمٍ وَبَنِينَ أَمَدَّكُم بِأَنْعَـٰمٍ۝

692
00:52:06,463 --> 00:52:07,947
أَمَدَّكُم بِأَنْعَـٰمٍ

693
00:52:08,288 --> 00:52:11,233
He has provided you with cattle.

694
00:52:12,009 --> 00:52:16,566
In modern terms, we refer to that as livestock, animal resources.

695
00:52:17,375 --> 00:52:22,780
So they were wealthy in terms of livestock, they had abundance of livestock.

696
00:52:23,502 --> 00:52:24,635
 وَبَنِينَ

697
00:52:25,373 --> 00:52:26,706
and children

698
00:52:27,349 --> 00:52:30,794
and that is what we call, in modern terms, manpower.

699
00:52:31,087 --> 00:52:35,652
وَجَنَّـٰتٍ وَعُيُونٍ۝

700
00:52:35,692 --> 00:52:36,716
وَجَنَّـٰتٍ

701
00:52:37,303 --> 00:52:38,298
gardens

702
00:52:38,660 --> 00:52:41,973
and that is what we call, in modern terms, agriculture.

703
00:52:42,790 --> 00:52:43,711
 وَعُيُونٍ

704
00:52:43,965 --> 00:52:46,108
and that is water resources.

705
00:52:47,084 --> 00:52:50,690
So Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ has given them livestock,

706
00:52:51,007 --> 00:52:52,579
and has given them manpower,

707
00:52:52,912 --> 00:52:54,841
and has given them agriculture,

708
00:52:55,095 --> 00:52:59,772
and has provided them with an ample supply, good supply of water.

709
00:53:00,327 --> 00:53:01,945
That is ʿAd(عاد)’s society,

710
00:53:02,214 --> 00:53:06,453
and then they as individuals, Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ gave them a powerful structure.

711
00:53:07,310 --> 00:53:09,922
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ has said about them;

712
00:53:10,383 --> 00:53:16,049
أَتَبْنُونَ بِكُلِّ رِيعٍ ءَايَةً تَعْبَثُونَ ۝

713
00:53:16,383 --> 00:53:21,734
وَتَتَّخِذُونَ مَصَانِعَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَخْلُدُونَ ۝

714
00:53:21,972 --> 00:53:27,032
 وَإِذَا بَطَشْتُم بَطَشْتُمْ جَبَّارِينَ ۝

715
00:53:27,313 --> 00:53:31,281
 فَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُونِ۝

716
00:53:31,686 --> 00:53:36,586
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ said, in these Ayaat(آيات),

717
00:53:37,673 --> 00:53:44,948
they became so luxurious and so wealthy that they were spending their money in a wasteful way, Israf(اسراف).

718
00:53:45,979 --> 00:53:47,122
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

719
00:53:47,162 --> 00:53:50,329
أَتَبْنُونَ بِكُلِّ رِيعٍ ءَايَةً تَعْبَثُونَ۝

720
00:53:52,011 --> 00:53:54,966
The people of ʿAd(عاد) had so much additional wealth,

721
00:53:56,085 --> 00:54:00,751
they started to fall into the trap that rich nations fall into,

722
00:54:00,957 --> 00:54:04,886
and that is using your money for pride and arrogance.

723
00:54:05,198 --> 00:54:11,722
 After you satisfy your basic needs, food and drink and shelter, and you have additional money,

724
00:54:12,865 --> 00:54:17,649
if there is no Eeman(إيمان) to spend it the right way, then it will be spent in evil.

725
00:54:18,856 --> 00:54:25,481
The people of ʿAd(عاد) had this additional wealth, so they started building monuments over mountains.

726
00:54:25,806 --> 00:54:29,227
They would build on top of these mountains monuments

727
00:54:30,187 --> 00:54:36,609
that they will not use for living, they don’t need them, they’re just building them for pride, to show off.

728
00:54:37,085 --> 00:54:38,164
And Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

729
00:54:38,244 --> 00:54:39,236
 تَعْبَثُونَ

730
00:54:39,895 --> 00:54:44,288
Do you build high palaces in every high place while you do not live in them?

731
00:54:44,431 --> 00:54:45,856
 Wastefully - ʿAbath(عبث),

732
00:54:46,010 --> 00:54:47,804
ʿAbath(عبث) means when you waste something.

733
00:54:48,724 --> 00:54:53,380
So they had so much wealth, so much disposable money,

734
00:54:53,515 --> 00:54:56,658
that they started building these monuments on top of mountains.

735
00:54:58,242 --> 00:55:01,063
وَتَتَّخِذُونَ مَصَانِعَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَخْلُدُونَ۝

736
00:55:01,618 --> 00:55:04,396
These buildings on top of mountains, they don’t use them for living.

737
00:55:04,745 --> 00:55:07,341
But the dwellings that they built for themselves,

738
00:55:07,697 --> 00:55:12,840
they used to build it in a way as if they’re going to live forever, so strong and powerful.

739
00:55:13,257 --> 00:55:16,391
وَتَتَّخِذُونَ مَصَانِعَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَخْلُدُونَ۝

740
00:55:16,741 --> 00:55:21,452
And do you get yourselves palaces as if you will live forever?

741
00:55:21,777 --> 00:55:29,364
The way they would build their palaces shows that they used to think that they’re gonna live forever.

742
00:55:30,091 --> 00:55:38,730
They used to build it so strong and well constructed, very strong structure, as if they are going to live on the face of the earth forever.

743
00:55:39,413 --> 00:55:43,901
And Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ when He destroyed them, He destroyed them and He didn’t leave anything that they left

744
00:55:44,079 --> 00:55:46,479
anything that they built, it was all destroyed.

745
00:55:48,130 --> 00:55:50,781
وَإِذَا بَطَشْتُم بَطَشْتُمْ جَبَّارِينَ۝

746
00:55:50,971 --> 00:55:53,201
And when you seize, you seize like tyrants.

747
00:55:53,511 --> 00:55:54,577
They were powerful.

748
00:55:55,140 --> 00:55:57,283
Even though this nation was wealthy

749
00:55:58,338 --> 00:56:01,386
some nations, when they become wealthy, they become weak

750
00:56:02,509 --> 00:56:05,113
but the people of ʿAd(عاد), they were keeping their strength.

751
00:56:05,153 --> 00:56:08,443
Even though they were very wealthy and luxurious, they were still very powerful,

752
00:56:08,686 --> 00:56:13,421
and then when they would attack any neighbours, they would completely destroy them.

753
00:56:13,500 --> 00:56:14,214
Tyrants.

754
00:56:14,334 --> 00:56:17,564
بطش وَإِذَا بَطَشْتُم بَطَشْتُمْ جَبَّارِينَ۝

755
00:56:18,540 --> 00:56:20,656
So there’s a difference between the people of ʿAd(عاد) and Thamud(ثمود‎).

756
00:56:20,696 --> 00:56:23,674
ʿAd(عاد) were powerful tyrants.

757
00:56:24,856 --> 00:56:30,986
All of these things combined, when you put them together, Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

758
00:56:31,074 --> 00:56:36,709
عَادٍ إِرَمَ ذَاتِ ٱلْعِمَادِ ۝ ٱلَّتِى لَمْ يُخْلَقْ مِثْلُهَا فِى ٱلْبِلَـٰدِ۝

759
00:56:38,169 --> 00:56:39,153
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

760
00:56:39,193 --> 00:56:41,377
عَادٍ إِرَمَ ذَاتِ ٱلْعِمَادِ

761
00:56:41,744 --> 00:56:47,768
The land of pillars which Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ has created no land similar to it.

762
00:56:48,617 --> 00:56:54,118
This society and these people, Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ did not create anyone similar to them.

763
00:56:54,999 --> 00:56:57,734
When you put all these things together,

764
00:56:58,441 --> 00:57:03,199
all of these different resources that Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ has given them, all of these blessings together,

765
00:57:03,445 --> 00:57:12,636
they were able to build a civilization and nation and society that was unsurpassed by anyone in their time.

766
00:57:13,795 --> 00:57:16,937
The like of which were not created in the land.

767
00:57:17,049 --> 00:57:18,194
No one was like them.

768
00:57:19,668 --> 00:57:21,890
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ sent to them Hud(هود‎).

769
00:57:22,375 --> 00:57:27,414
وَإِلَىٰ عَادٍ أَخَاهُمْ هُودًا۝

770
00:57:27,639 --> 00:57:29,544
And to ʿAd(عاد) their brother Hud(هود).

771
00:57:29,679 --> 00:57:32,338
He was called their brother because he’s from them.

772
00:57:32,893 --> 00:57:34,330
What was his message?

773
00:57:34,973 --> 00:57:36,097
The same message of Nuh(نوح).

774
00:57:36,272 --> 00:57:50,741
قَالَ يَـٰقَوْمِ ٱعْبُدُوا ٱللَّهَ مَا لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَـٰهٍ غَيْرُهُۥٓ ۖ إِنْ أَنتُمْ إِلَّا مُفْتَرُونَ۝

775
00:57:50,987 --> 00:57:56,050
O my people, worship Allah; you have no other God but Him.

776
00:57:56,256 --> 00:58:00,597
Certainly you do nothing but invent lies.

777
00:58:01,687 --> 00:58:05,034
These gods who you are worshiping are lies.

778
00:58:05,931 --> 00:58:10,159
See, the Ambiya(أنبياء) of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ they are straightforward

779
00:58:10,436 --> 00:58:13,797
because that is part of the Amanah(أمانة), Amanat At-Tabligh(أمانة التبليغ),

780
00:58:14,527 --> 00:58:20,590
the trust that Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ has given them and the responsibility of conveying the truth, and that is why they say;

781
00:58:20,749 --> 00:58:22,455
إِنِّى لَكُمْ رَسُولٌ أَمِينٌ۝

782
00:58:22,746 --> 00:58:25,040
He said: I am a trustworthy.

783
00:58:25,596 --> 00:58:27,126
وَأَنَا لَكُمْ نَاصِحٌ أَمِينٌ۝

784
00:58:27,166 --> 00:58:27,691
And he said;

785
00:58:27,818 --> 00:58:30,958
And I came to you to advise you with honesty.

786
00:58:31,218 --> 00:58:32,400
So they are straightforward.

787
00:58:32,440 --> 00:58:33,837
He told them: “You are lying,”

788
00:58:36,242 --> 00:58:37,170
and he told them;

789
00:58:37,496 --> 00:58:46,177
وَيَـٰقَوْمِ ٱسْتَغْفِرُوا رَبَّكُمْ ثُمَّ تُوبُوا إِلَيْهِ

790
00:58:46,415 --> 00:58:52,722
O my people, seek forgiveness from Allah سبحانه وتعالى and then repent to Him.

791
00:58:53,055 --> 00:58:55,972
And we just talked last night about Nuh(نوح), he told his people the same thing.

792
00:58:56,226 --> 00:58:59,155
He told them: Ask Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ to forgive you,

793
00:58:59,345 --> 00:59:02,990
and we talked about the things that they will be given if they ask Allah for forgiveness.

794
00:59:03,298 --> 00:59:06,292
And here, Hud (هود‎) is also telling them additional things. He said;

795
00:59:07,072 --> 00:59:23,325
وَيَـٰقَوْمِ ٱسْتَغْفِرُوا۟ رَبَّكُمْ ثُمَّ تُوبُوٓا۟ إِلَيْهِ يُرْسِلِ ٱلسَّمَآءَ عَلَيْكُم مِّدْرَارًا

796
00:59:24,144 --> 00:59:44,548
 ثُمَّ تُوبُوٓا۟ إِلَيْهِ يُرْسِلِ ٱلسَّمَآءَ عَلَيْكُم مِّدْرَارًا وَيَزِدْكُمْ قُوَّةً إِلَىٰ قُوَّتِكُمْ وَلَا تَتَوَلَّوْا۟ مُجْرِمِينَ۝

797
00:59:45,064 --> 00:59:50,174
O my people, ask forgiveness of your Lord and then repent to Him;

798
00:59:50,515 --> 00:59:57,735
He will send you from the sky abundant rain and add strength to your strength.

799
00:59:59,759 --> 01:00:04,562
So with Istighfar(إستغفار), you would become more powerful than you are now.

800
01:00:05,032 --> 01:00:10,405
They were already powerful and strong; if they ask Allah for forgiveness, Allah will give them more power and strength.

801
01:00:11,905 --> 01:00:16,294
This tells us something, it’s telling us that we’re not making enough Istighfar(ٱستغفار‎) to Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎.

802
01:00:17,159 --> 01:00:22,085
If we were making Istighfar(ٱستغفار‎) as we should, our situation would not be the way it is today.

803
01:00:25,037 --> 01:00:26,855
What was their response?

804
01:00:27,775 --> 01:00:29,196
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

805
01:00:30,092 --> 01:00:48,492
قَالُوا۟ يَـٰهُودُ مَا جِئْتَنَا بِبَيِّنَةٍ وَمَا نَحْنُ بِتَارِكِىٓ ءَالِهَتِنَا عَن قَوْلِكَ وَمَا نَحْنُ لَكَ بِمُؤْمِنِينَ۝

806
01:00:48,817 --> 01:00:51,518
They said: “O Hud(هود), no evidence have you brought us,

807
01:00:51,733 --> 01:00:57,087
and we shall not leave our gods for your mere say, and we are not believers in you.

808
01:00:57,127 --> 01:00:57,925
They rejected.

809
01:00:58,211 --> 01:00:59,631
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

810
01:01:00,092 --> 01:01:03,494
كَذَّبَتْ عَادٌ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ۝

811
01:01:03,589 --> 01:01:06,724
Ad(عاد) denied the Messengers.

812
01:01:07,049 --> 01:01:08,787
How many Messengers did they receive?

813
01:01:10,097 --> 01:01:11,207
One

814
01:01:11,920 --> 01:01:12,953
but Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ said;

815
01:01:13,033 --> 01:01:14,937
كَذَّبَتْ عَادٌ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ۝

816
01:01:15,239 --> 01:01:19,062
The people of ʿAd(عاد) have disbelieved in the Messengers.

817
01:01:19,235 --> 01:01:20,672
Plural, not One,

818
01:01:22,014 --> 01:01:23,709
but they only received one Messenger.

819
01:01:24,312 --> 01:01:25,820
How come it’s made plural?

820
01:01:28,161 --> 01:01:33,534
If you refuse one Messenger, it is as if you refused them all

821
01:01:33,971 --> 01:01:36,820
because all of the Messengers came with the same message.

822
01:01:37,669 --> 01:01:40,564
So if you refuse the message of Hud(هود‎),

823
01:01:40,727 --> 01:01:43,426
it is as if you refused the message of everyone.

824
01:01:44,116 --> 01:01:51,466
If you refuse the message of Muhammad ﷺ, it would not suffice you to believe in ʿIsa(عيسى‎) or Musa(موسی) or any other Nabi(نبي‎).

825
01:01:52,156 --> 01:01:58,236
If you disbelieve in one Nabi(نبي‎), in one Rasul(رسول‎), it is as if you have disbelieved in all of them.

826
01:01:59,450 --> 01:02:02,386
So even, let’s assume even that today,

827
01:02:02,513 --> 01:02:08,271
there’s somebody who believes in ʿIsa(عيسى‎) and Musa(موسی) and believes in Allah only and doesn’t believe in any other god,

828
01:02:08,517 --> 01:02:12,016
but he does not believe in Muhammad ﷺ that is not Islam.

829
01:02:12,969 --> 01:02:18,262
You have to believe in all of the Ambiya(أنبياء) of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎, from Adam(آدم) until Muhammad ﷺ.

830
01:02:20,469 --> 01:02:23,671
So they disbelieved in Hud(هود‎) only, but Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ said;

831
01:02:23,735 --> 01:02:25,298
كَذَّبَتْ عَادٌ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ۝

832
01:02:25,338 --> 01:02:27,616
They disbelieved in all of the Messengers.

833
01:02:29,933 --> 01:02:33,105
And they started accusing him, and that will happen to every Nabi(نبي‎).

834
01:02:33,867 --> 01:02:35,716
They accused him of insanity.

835
01:02:36,700 --> 01:02:37,406
They said;

836
01:02:37,557 --> 01:02:46,282
إِن نَّقُولُ إِلَّا ٱعْتَرَىٰكَ بَعْضُ ءَالِهَتِنَا بِسُوءٍ

837
01:02:46,759 --> 01:02:51,905
All that we say is that some of our gods have seized you with madness.

838
01:02:52,341 --> 01:02:57,780
They said: Our gods have caused you insanity, you’re mad.

839
01:02:58,293 --> 01:03:03,015
And they accused him of Sufaha(سفاها) and they accused him of lying.

840
01:03:03,404 --> 01:03:32,090
قَالَ ٱلْمَلَأُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ مِن قَوْمِهِۦٓ إِنَّا لَنَرَىٰكَ فِى سَفَاهَةٍ وَإِنَّا لَنَظُنُّكَ مِنَ ٱلْكَـٰذِبِينَ۝

841
01:03:32,304 --> 01:03:35,502
The leaders of those who disbelieved among his people said;

842
01:03:35,669 --> 01:03:41,334
Verily, we see you in foolishness, and verily, we think you are one of the liars.

843
01:03:42,302 --> 01:03:45,461
And notice who are the ones who are saying this? Al-Mala(ٱلملأ), the leaders.

844
01:03:46,461 --> 01:03:57,492
وَقَالَ ٱلْمَلَأُ مِن قَوْمِهِ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ وَكَذَّبُوا۟ بِلِقَآءِ ٱلْـَٔاخِرَةِ وَأَتْرَفْنَـٰهُمْ فِى ٱلْحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنْيَا

845
01:03:57,790 --> 01:04:07,428
مَا هَـٰذَآ إِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُكُمْ يَأْكُلُ مِمَّا تَأْكُلُونَ مِنْهُ وَيَشْرَبُ مِمَّا تَشْرَبُونَ۝

846
01:04:07,904 --> 01:04:12,775
And the chiefs of his people who disbelieved and denied the meeting in the Hereafter.

847
01:04:13,069 --> 01:04:14,497
So they disbelieve in Akhirah(آخرة)

848
01:04:15,156 --> 01:04:19,402
and to whom We had given the luxuries and comforts of this life.

849
01:04:19,767 --> 01:04:22,815
Luxuries and comforts did not do them any good,

850
01:04:23,237 --> 01:04:26,904
did not mean that they were intelligent, did not mean that they were better.

851
01:04:28,292 --> 01:04:29,297
They had luxuries

852
01:04:29,523 --> 01:04:30,268
  أَتْرَفْنَـٰهُمْ

853
01:04:30,308 --> 01:04:34,967
they had luxuries; nevertheless, their minds were not sufficient enough to lead them to the truth.

854
01:04:35,470 --> 01:04:40,200
So, wealth and money and luxury does not mean anything in the standard of Eeman(إيمان).

855
01:04:41,399 --> 01:04:43,914
You could have all the wealth in the world and refuse the truth,

856
01:04:44,196 --> 01:04:48,511
and you could have nothing, nevertheless, you would be intelligent enough to know that this is Al-haqq(الحق).

857
01:04:49,445 --> 01:04:50,763
 They had a lot.

858
01:04:50,803 --> 01:04:52,511
وَأَتْرَفْنَـٰهُمْ فِى ٱلْحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنْيَا

859
01:04:52,551 --> 01:04:55,072
We had given them luxuries, but they said;

860
01:04:55,644 --> 01:04:58,023
He is no more than a human being like you.

861
01:04:58,149 --> 01:05:01,800
He eats of that which you eat and drinks of what you drink.

862
01:05:02,007 --> 01:05:04,419
They said: “How can we follow a man who eats and drinks like us?

863
01:05:04,999 --> 01:05:12,139
وَلَئِنْ أَطَعْتُم بَشَرًا مِّثْلَكُمْ إِنَّكُمْ إِذًا لَّخَـٰسِرُونَ۝

864
01:05:12,869 --> 01:05:17,867
If you were to obey a human being like yourselves, then verily, you indeed would be losers.

865
01:05:18,335 --> 01:05:31,354
أَيَعِدُكُمْ أَنَّكُمْ إِذَا مِتُّمْ وَكُنتُمْ تُرَابًا وَعِظَـٰمًا أَنَّكُم مُّخْرَجُونَ۝

866
01:05:32,032 --> 01:05:37,937
Does he promise you that when you have died and have became dust and bones, you shall come out alive?

867
01:05:38,024 --> 01:05:39,835
They refuse to believe in the Resurrection.

868
01:05:40,097 --> 01:05:41,351
Materialistic thinking.

869
01:05:42,327 --> 01:05:46,875
هَيْهَاتَ هَيْهَاتَ لِمَا تُوعَدُونَ۝

870
01:05:47,057 --> 01:05:50,185
Far, very far, is that which you are promised.

871
01:05:50,716 --> 01:06:00,221
إِنْ هِىَ إِلَّا حَيَاتُنَا ٱلدُّنْيَا نَمُوتُ وَنَحْيَا وَمَا نَحْنُ بِمَبْعُوثِينَ۝

872
01:06:00,617 --> 01:06:06,808
There is nothing but our life of this world, we die and we live, and we are not going to be resurrected.

873
01:06:06,942 --> 01:06:17,507
إِنْ هُوَ إِلَّا رَجُلٌ ٱفْتَرَىٰ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ كَذِبًا وَمَا نَحْنُ لَهُۥ بِمُؤْمِنِينَ۝

874
01:06:17,761 --> 01:06:21,340
He is only a man who has invented a lie against Allah,

875
01:06:21,666 --> 01:06:23,615
but we are not going to believe in him.

876
01:06:23,964 --> 01:06:28,536
Now they are accusing Hud(هود‎) of lying against Allah سبحانه وتعالى.‎

877
01:06:28,591 --> 01:06:32,555
They are claiming that they are the true believers in Allah and he is lying against Allah.

878
01:06:35,166 --> 01:06:37,889
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

